body:
[Theorem thm:alternating2Necce of arXiv:2608.24731, 'Optimal Alternating Regret for Online Learning and Games\thanks{Authors are alphabetically'] Suppose that in the above alternating learning dynamics,  the $x$-player and the $y$-player use OCO algorithms with alternating regret bound $\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(x)$ and $\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(y)$, respectively. Then 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[1.] for a zero-sum game,  the averaged strategy $(1/T\sum_{t=1}^T \boldsymbol{x}_t, 1/T\sum_{t=1}^T \boldsymbol{y}_t)$ is an $\epsilon$-NE with $\epsilon = O((\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(x)+ \operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(y))/T)$;
        \item[2.] for a general-sum game, the uniform distribution over $\{(\boldsymbol{x}_t, \boldsymbol{y}_t), (\boldsymbol{x}_{t+1}, \boldsymbol{y}_t)\}_{t \in [T]}$ is an $\epsilon$-CCE with $\epsilon = O(\max\{\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(x), \operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(y)\}/T)$
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

