[Theorem burk_thm of arXiv:2506.09364, 'A collection of results relating the geometry of plane domains and the exit time of planar'] Suppose $h$ is a positive function on a domain $D$ satisfying $(i)$ and $(ii)$ above. Suppose also that

    \begin{enumerate}
    \item[$(iii)$] There is a constant $C>0$ such that $h(z) \leq C(1+|z|^2)$ for all $z \in D$.
\end{enumerate}

Then $h(a) = E_a[T(D)]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $0<\sigma<1$, $\beta>0$, and define $N_h:=h^{-\sigma/2}$ for $0<h\le1$.  Then there are constants $C,c>0$ such that for all $x\in H^{\alpha+\beta}$,
\begin{equation}

\norm{P_{>N_h}x}_{H^\alpha}
\le
C h^{\sigma\beta/2}
\norm{x}_{H^{\alpha+\beta}},
\end{equation}
and for all $x\in H^\alpha$,
\begin{equation}

\norm{S_h^{-1}P_{\le N_h}x}_{H^\alpha}
\le
\exp(c h^{1-\sigma})
\norm{x}_{H^\alpha}.
\end{equation}
Here $S_h^{-1}P_{\le N_h}$ is defined spectrally on the finite-dimensional range of $P_{\le N_h}$.

