[Proposition prop:prop3.6 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, any triplet of inverse temperatures $\beta, \beta_1 , \beta_2 \in (0 , \infty)$, any percolation configuration $r \in \{0 , 1 \}^{\Lambda_L}$, and any pair of vertices $x , y \in \Lambda_L$, one has the convergences: 
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, n, \beta, r}^{\mathrm{XY}} =  \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, \beta,r}^{\mathrm{Vil}}
    \end{equation*}
    and
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, n, \beta_1 , \beta_2, r}^{\mathrm{XY}} =  \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, \beta_1 , \beta_2, r}^{\mathrm{XY/Vil}}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

