body:
[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] For every $\eta,\delta>0$ and every $\rho\in(0,\frac12)$, there exists $n_{\eta,\delta,\rho}\in\N$ such that, for every $n\geq n_{\eta,\delta,\rho}$, the region
    \begin{equation}
        \left\{
            (a,b)\in\R_+^2:
            ab\leq n^{-\frac23-\eta}
        \right\}
        \cup
        \left\{
            (a,b)\in\R_+^2:
            ab\leq\frac12-\rho,\quad
            \min\{a,b\}\leq n^{-\frac12-\delta}
        \right\}
    \end{equation}
    is contained in the frame set of the $n$-th Hermite function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 1 of arXiv:2609.02105, 'Contact fundamental forms and \\ adjoint varieties'] Let $W$ be a vector space and let $\Sym W^* = \oplus_{k \in \Z} \Sym^k W^*$ be the graded ring of polynomial functions on $W$, regarded as an algebraic variety.  Here, we use the convention $\Sym^k W^* =0$ if $k<0$.
\begin{itemize} \item[(i)] For each $w \in W$, let $\p_w$ be the vector field on $W$ corresponding to $w$ under the canonical trivialization $T W = W \times W$ and regard it as an operator $\p_w \in \Hom(\Sym W^*, \Sym W^*) $ sending $\Sym^{k} W^*$ to $\Sym^{k-1} W^*$ for any $k$.  \item[(ii)]  A finite-dimensional graded vector subspace $$S = \oplus_{k \in \Z} S^k \subset \Sym W^*, \ S^k \subset \Sym^k W^*,$$ is called a {\em symbol system  on $W$} if $S^0 = \C, \ S^1 = W^*$ and  $\p_w S^k \subset S^{k-1}$ for any $k\geq 2$ and $ w \in W$. 
 \end{itemize}

[Lemma CountingCoarseGrains of arXiv:2605.18744, 'Lattice random-field Widom--Rowlinson models'] There exists $C>0$ such that for all $n\in \mathbb{Z}_{>0}$ and $1\le k\le N(n)$
\begin{align*}
    M_{n,k}\le \exp(Ckn2^{-(d-1)k}).
\end{align*}

