[Lemma lem:shift-cumulants of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $\epsilon_1,\ldots,\epsilon_n\in\{1,-1\}$ and $b_1,\ldots,b_n\in\mathcal{B}_0$. Put $p_j=\epsilon_1+\cdots+\epsilon_j$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \kappa_n^{\mathcal{B}_0}(u^{\epsilon_1}b_1,\ldots,u^{\epsilon_n}b_n)=\kappa_n^{\mathbb C}(z^{\epsilon_1},\ldots,z^{\epsilon_n})\prod_{j=1}^n\alpha^{p_j}(b_j).
\end{equation}

