body:
[Thm 3.2 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\xi, \xi'\in L_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^k)$, both $g$ and $g'$ be the generator of BSDEs satisfying assumptions (A:H4 of the paper) and (A:H5 of the paper), and $(Y_\cdot,Z_\cdot)$ and $(Y_\cdot',Z_\cdot')$ be the weighted $L^p$ solution of BSDE$(\xi,\tau,g)$ and BSDE$(\xi',\tau,g')$, respectively, in the space of $H_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$.
Then there exists a constant $C_{p,\theta}>0$ depending only on $p$ and $\theta$ such that
\begin{align*}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{s\in[0,\tau]}\left(e^{p \int_{0}^{s}\rho_r{\rm d}r}|Y_s-Y_s'|^p\right)\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^{\tau} e^{2\int_0^s \rho_r{\rm d}r}|Z_s-Z_s'|^2{\rm d}s\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}\right]\\
&\ \ \leq  C_{p,\theta}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[e^{p \int_{0}^{\tau}\rho_r{\rm d}r}|\xi-\xi'|^p\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^\tau e^{\int_0^s\rho_r{\rm d}r}\left|g(t,Y'_t,Z'_t)-g'(t,Y'_t,Z'_t)\right|{\rm d}s\right)^p\right]\right).
\end{split}
\end{align*}

