[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $r$ be an exponentially summable finite signed measure on $\N^d$. For every compact set $K\subset\R^d$,

\begin{equation}
\sup_{k\in\mathcal W_a(K)}
 a^{(d-1)/2}
\left|\sum_{|u|_1>R}U_C(k-u)r(u)\right|
\xrightarrow[R\to\infty]{}0
\end{equation}

uniformly for all sufficiently large $a$, where $U_C(v)=0$ if $v\notin\N^d$. Consequently, the asymptotic for $U_r$ follows from \eqref{eq:S22-renewal-local} by finite truncation.

