[Thm 2 of arXiv:2605.02420, '\textbf{Large time behavior of critical marked Hawkes processes with heavy tailed marks an'] Suppose that $\beta\in(0,1)$ and the Assumptions \ref{ass:beta_general}  and \ref{ass:beta_integrable} are satisfied.
 Then the process $Y_T$ defined by \eqref{e:YT} with 
 \begin{equation}
  F_T=T^{1+\beta}
 \end{equation}
converges in the sense of finite dimensional distributions and in law in $D([0,\infty))$ equipped with $M_1$ topology to $K^{-1}L_{1/(1+\beta)}$,
where
$L_{ 1/(1+\beta)}$ is a $\frac 1{1+\beta}$-stable subordinator, that is $L_{1/1+\beta}$  is a nondecreasing process with stationary and independent increments such that its one dimensional distributions have the following Laplace transform:
\begin{equation*}
 E\exp\left\{-\theta L_{1/(1+\beta)}(t)\right\}=\exp\left\{-t\theta^{1/(1+\beta)}\right\}, \qquad t\ge 0, \theta\ge 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2511.00764, 'Further Developments on Stochastic Dominance for Convex\\ Combinations of Infinite-Mean Ra'] \

Let $m\in \N$ be fixed with $m \ge 2$.
