[Lemma lem_limit_F of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] In the weakly subcritical regime $({\bf m}\in(-\sigma^2,0)).$ Using the time-dependent function $G_t(y, v)$ defined in (equation Gt_def_time of the paper), let $\nu_{\Phi, t}$ be a time-dependent measure on $\mathbb{R}$ with its density defined precisely by $G_t$:
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{\nu_{\Phi, t}(\mathrm{d} x)}{\mathrm{d} x} := \frac{\beta^2 \lambda^\beta}{2} \int_0^{\gamma^{-1/\beta}} \mathrm{e}^{-\beta(1-\eta)x} w^{-1} G_t\left(\mathrm{e}^{-\beta x}w^\beta, \frac{\lambda^\beta}{2}(w^{-\beta}-\gamma)\right) \mathrm{d} w.
\end{eqnarray}
Then $F(t) = \mathbb{E}^z[1-\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda Z_t}]$ can be exactly represented as an integral with respect to this measure:
\begin{eqnarray*}
F(t) = \int_{-\infty}^\infty \bigl(1 - \mathrm{e}^{-z \mathrm{e}^x}\bigr) \mathrm{e}^{-\beta\eta x}\,\nu_{\Phi, t}(\mathrm{d} x).
\end{eqnarray*}
Furthermore, as $t \to \infty$, the scaled density of the measure converges pointwise:
\begin{eqnarray*}
\lim _{t \rightarrow \infty} t^{3/2} \mathrm{e}^{\frac{{\bf m}^2}{2 \sigma^2} t} \frac{\nu_{\Phi, t}(\mathrm{d} x)}{\mathrm{d} x} = \frac{4\sqrt 2}{\sigma^3\beta^3\sqrt{ \pi }} \frac{\nu_\Phi(\mathrm{d} x)}{\mathrm{d} x},
\end{eqnarray*}
and consequently,
\begin{eqnarray}
\lim _{t \rightarrow \infty} t^{3/2} \mathrm{e}^{\frac{{\bf m}^2}{2 \sigma^2} t} F(t) = \frac{4\sqrt 2}{\sigma^3\beta^3\sqrt{ \pi }} \Phi(z, \lambda).
\end{eqnarray}

