body:
[Theorem thm:GW of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] If   the variance profile of the random matrix  \(H\) defined in  Definition (def:inhomo of the paper) 
satisfies  
\begin{equation}
    \sum_{j}\sigma_{ij}^2=1, \quad 0< c_N < N\,\sigma_{ij}^2 < C_N< \infty,
\end{equation}
then under the constraint \begin{equation} 
    \frac{C_N}{c_N}\, \theta\, \log N\;\ll\;N^{\frac{1}{3}},
\end{equation}
  the edge universality in Theorem~(thm:main_thm of the paper) holds for \(H\).

