        \item If $\bm{p} \in \TAC[2]$, and $\sigX[]\,, \sigY[] \in \eTA[2]\,$, then $\bracket{\bm{p}}{\sigX[] \otimes \sigY[]} = \bracket{~_{\sigX[]}|\bm{p}}{\sigY[]} = \bracket{\bm{p}|_{\sigY[]}}{\sigX[]}\,$.
        \item If $\bm{p}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}} \in \mathcal{A}_{\sigX[]}$ for all ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}} \in V$, then $\bracket{\bm{p}}{\sigX[]\otimes {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}} = \bracket{~_{\sigX[]}|\bm{p}}{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}} = \bracket{\bm{p}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}}}{\sigX[]}\,$, for all $\bm p \in \eTAC[2]\,$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Proposition prop hitting balls of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] Almost surely, for all $x, y \in \BD_\BQ$, for all $t_1 \le D(\SCL(x), \SCL(y)) $,
