body:
[Theorem t:hardcheeger of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let $G=(V,\mathcal{E})$ be a finite graph, respecting Convention (conv;simple of the paper) and such that $|V|=N$, and let $\mu_k$ be the $k$-th smallest eigenvalue of its normalized Laplacian ${\ensuremath{\mathcal L}} $, for $k=2,\ldots,N$. Then, there exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that, for every $k=2,...,N$, there exists a partition $S_1,...,S_k$ of $V$ with nonempty subsets verifying
\begin{equation*}
\max_{i=1,\ldots, k} \varphi(S_i)\leq Ck^4 \, \sqrt{\mu_k}\,.
\end{equation*}    
{In particular, one has that $\varphi_k(G) \leq Ck^4 \, \sqrt{\mu_k}$.} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:technical of arXiv:2606.30475, 'Ancestries in random $d$-DAGs'] With notation as before, suppose there exists a constant $\kappa>0$ such that
 \begin{equation}
  0\leq q_n(i,j) \leq \kappa \frac{j}{n^{d+1}} \frac{i^d}{(1-j/n)^d}
 \end{equation}
 for all $n\geq 1$, $i\in[n]$, and $j\in[n-i]$. Moreover assume that $n q_n(i,j)\to \hat q(\alpha,\beta)$ for all $i$ and $j$ such that $in^{-(d-1)/d}\to \alpha >0$ and $j/n\to \beta \in(0,1)$. Then
 \begin{multline}
  n^{-\frac{d-1}{d}} \sum_{i=1}^n \sum_{j=1}^{n-i} q_n(i,j) \prod_{k=1}^{j-1} \left[1-\bigg(\frac{i}{n-k}\bigg)^d\,\right]\\
  \to \int_0^\infty \int_0^1 \hat q(\alpha,\beta) e^{-\frac{\alpha^d}{(d-1)}\big((1-\beta)^{1-d}-1\big)} \,\mathrm{d}\beta \,\mathrm{d}\alpha
 \end{multline}
 as $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

