[Lem 53 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$, $\beta\geq 0$, and $n\geq 1$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ which contains $\Lambda_{2n}$. Let $S\subset \Lambda_{n-1}$ containing $0$. Then,
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf P^{\emptyset,\emptyset}_{G,\beta}[0\connect{\n_1+\n_2\:}\partial \Lambda_n]\leq \sum_{\substack{u\in S\\v\notin S\\u\sim v}}\langle \sigma_0\sigma_u\rangle_{S,\beta}\beta\langle \sigma_v\sigma_0\rangle_{G,\beta}. 
\end{equation}

