[Prop 70 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $N\geq 0$ and $\beta>N + 1/2$.
Then, for every $\eta>0$,
as $\gamma\to 0^{+}$,
the following asymptotic expansion holds in $L^{2}(d\PP,\sigma(\Phi),H^{-\eta}(\C))$:
\begin{displaymath}
\ind_{D\setminus A}
V_{A}^{\beta} \exp\Big(-\dfrac{\gamma^{2}}{2} V_{A}\Big)
= 
\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}
\sum_{j=0}^{N} (-1)^{j}
\dfrac{\Gamma(\beta -j-1/2) \gamma^{2j+1 - 2\beta}}{2^{2j+1/2 - \beta} j!}
\,\psi_{2j+1,A}
+
o(\gamma^{2N+1 - 2\beta}).
\end{displaymath}

