[Prop of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] The following gives a way to sample the loops $\ell_0, \ldots, \ell_{k-1}$ given $\eta$.
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Start independent Markov chains $X^j$ at each $\eta_j$ and let \[T^j = \min \{n \geq 0: X^j_n \in \partial A_j\}.\]
        \item Let \[\rho^j = \max \{m<T^j: X^j_m = x_j\}.\]
        \item Output \[\ell_j = [X^j_0, X^j_1, \ldots, X^j_{\rho^j}].\]
    \end{itemize}

