[Lemma lem:UI of arXiv:2608.23135, 'Graph distance and effective resistance of the random walk trace in four and five dimensio'] For every fixed $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and every $1<p<3/2$,
\begin{equation*}

 \sup_{n\geq1}
 \mathbb E\left[\left(\frac{S_{n}^{\varepsilon}}{n^{2/3}}\right)^p\right]
 <\infty.
\end{equation*}
In particular, the family
$\{S_{n}^{\varepsilon}/n^{2/3}:n\geq1\}$ is uniformly integrable.

[Lem lem_variation_lower_bound of arXiv:2411.13964, 'Long-time analysis of a pair of on-lattice and continuous run-and-tumble particles with ja'] If $\sigma^1$ and
  $\sigma^2$ are independent Markov jump processes with the transition
  rates (fig:single_speed_transition_rates_slowman_2017 of the paper) then
\begin{align*}
\inf_{\sigma} \mathbb{P}_{\sigma} \left( \sup_{t_1 \le t_2 \le t^*} \left|\int_{t_1}^{t_2} (\sigma^2(s) - \sigma^1(s)) ds \right| \ge \ell \right) \ge \frac{1}{144} 
\end{align*}
where $t^* = 288  \left( \frac{1}{\alpha} + \frac{1}{\beta} \right) \left( 1 + \alpha^2 \ell^2 \right) $.

[Lemma lem:equivalencen of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] The following equivalence between norms holds for any $ \alpha >1 $
\begin{equ}
\sum_{k \in \mathbf{Z}^{2}_{*}} | k |^{-2 \alpha} \| e_{k} \varphi \|_{H^{- \alpha}}^{2} \simeq
\| \varphi \|^{2}_{H^{- \alpha} }  \;.
\end{equ}

