[Lemma L:tri_st of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Let $t > 0$, let $\theta < 0$, and let $\zeta \in \mathbb{R}$. Then, the following two inequalities hold
\begin{gather}
  \left|\int_t^{\infty} \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } x \; x^{\theta} \cos (x + \zeta) \right| \lesssim t^{\theta}. 
  \shortintertext{and}
   \left|\int_t^{\infty} \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } x \; x^{\theta} \cos (x  + \zeta)\right| \lesssim
  \begin{dcases}
  1,  & \theta > -1,\\
  1 + |\log(t)|, & \theta = -1,\\
   t^{\theta + 1}, & \theta < - 1;
  \end{dcases} 
\end{gather}
Moreover,~(equation E:ibp of the paper) remains valid when substituting the cosine with the sine function.

