[Lem 23 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $0\leq\theta\leq1$, $p_0,p_1,p_2>1$ and $s,s_1,s_2\geq0$ be such that 
    \[\frac{1}{p_0}=\frac{\theta}{p_1}+\frac{1-\theta}{p_2}\quad\text{and}\quad s=\theta s_1+(1-\theta) s_2.\] 
    Then
    \begin{align*}
        \Vert f\Vert_{W^{s,p_0}}\leq\Vert f\Vert_{W^{s_1,p_1}}^\theta \Vert f\Vert_{W^{s_2,p_2}}^{1-\theta}
    \end{align*}
    for all $f\in W^{s_1,p_1}\cap W^{s_2,p_2}$.

[Lemma 20 (Metric comparison on the Stiefel manifold) of arXiv:2608.17374, '\textbf{On the Pseudo-Mixing of Kac's Walk}'] Let $D$ be the Riemannian distance on $\mathrm{St}(n,k)$ induced by the Frobenius
inner product from the embedding $\mathrm{St}(n,k)\subset \mathbb{R}^{n\times k}$.
Then, for all $X,Y\in \mathrm{St}(n,k)$,
\begin{equation}

\|X-Y\|\leq D(X,Y).
\end{equation}
Moreover, there are universal constants $\rho_D>0$ and $C_D<\infty$, independent
of $n$ and $k$, such that whenever $\|X-Y\|\leq \rho_D$,
\begin{equation}

D(X,Y)\leq \|X-Y\|+C_D\|X-Y\|^2.
\end{equation}

