[Theorem LUE soft left2 of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Consider an LUE $L_{a,N}$. Suppose there exist $\Theta_1,~\Theta_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $0<\Theta_1\le\frac{N}{n}\le \Theta_2<1$ and $\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{N}{n}=\gamma\in(0,1)$ where $n=N+a$. Then on any $A\subset[s,+\infty)$ for $s>-\infty$, with the same parameters as in Theorem (LUE left soft of the paper), for $N\in\mathbb{N}$ large enough,
    \begin{equation}
W_1\left(\mathcal{N}_{L_{a,N}}^{LS},\mathcal{N}_{Ai}\right)\le\frac{g(s,\Theta_1,\Theta_2)e^{-s}}{N^{\frac{2}{3}}}
    \end{equation}
 where $g$ is nonincreasing with respect to $s$ for any fixed $\Theta_1$ and $\Theta_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2605.09372, 'Sharp weighted norm estimates for martingale square functions'] Let $1<p<\infty$. Given a matrix weight $W\in A_p$, we have
\begin{equation}
		\int_{\Omega}\sup_n \left[ \mathbb E_{n}\left(\big\|W^{\frac{1}{p}} \widehat{W}_{n}\big\|g\right)\right]^{p'}d\mathbb P\lesssim_{p,d}[W]_{A_p}^{p'}\|g\|_{L_{p'}}^{p'},\quad \forall\, 0\leq g\in L_{p'}.
	\end{equation}

