body:
[Definition def:fixedgenuschain of arXiv:2607.02410, 'Polynomial mixing for polygonal side matchings'] For positive integers $n \geq 2$ and $g \leq n/2$, let $\chorddiagrams{n}{g}$ be the set of all genus $g$ chord diagrams with $n$ chords. The \emph{fixed genus chord swap chain} on $\chorddiagrams{n}{g}$ is the Markov chain obtained by the following transition kernel:
	\begin{equation*}
		P(X,Y) = \begin{cases}
			\frac{1}{4 {n \choose 2}} & Y \text{ is a chord swap of $X$ and has the same genus as $X$} \\
			1 - \sum_{Z \in \chorddiagrams{n}{g} \backslash \{X\}} P(X,Z) & X=Y \, .
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation*}

[Prop Psi properties of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For any $\boldsymbol{F} \subset \mathbb{T}_N$ and $M_0>0$ such that 
    (equation eq: cost of inserting loops not large of the paper) holds, and
    for any $(\boldsymbol{F},\varepsilon,M_0)$-good path collection $\mathcal{A}$, there exists a mapping $\Psi$ from $\mathcal{A}$ to $2^{\Omega_{T_4}}$ such that:
    \begin{subequations}

        \begin{align}
            & \text{For any } \omega \in \mathcal{A} \text{ and } \widetilde{\omega} \in \Psi(\omega) \text{, we have } \mathbb{T}_N \subset \widetilde{\omega}[0,T_4] ;\\ 
            &\text{For any } \omega \in \mathcal{A}\text{, we have }|\Psi(\omega)| \geq (2d)^{T_4-T_3 - J(\boldsymbol{F},M_0)};   \\
            &\text{For any } \omega,\omega' \in \mathcal{A} \text{ and } \omega \neq \omega' \text{, we have }\Psi(\omega) \cap \Psi(\omega') = \emptyset ,
        \end{align}
    \end{subequations}
    where $J(\boldsymbol{F},M_0)$ is defined in (equation cost of inserting loops of the paper).

