[Proposition prop:OPRE-temporal-extinction of arXiv:2507.00329, 'Oriented bond-site percolation in random environment and contact processes with periodic r'] Assume that $(\nu_{t,t+1})_{t\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq0}}$ is a family of i.i.d.\ random variables with heavier than exponential tails, i.e.,
    \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{s\to\infty} c^s\mathbb{P}(\nu_{0,1} > s) =\infty \qquad\text{ for all } c>1.
    \end{equation}
    Then, for every $p\in(0,1)$, the oriented percolation model with temporal stretches almost-surely does not contain an infinite open path. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

