[Thm 38 ({\hspace{1pt}\cite[Theorem~1) of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] {CamiaJiangNewman21}}] Let $d>4$. There exist $M >2$ and $c_0>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$, and every $x,y\in \Lambda_{2n}$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\langle\sigma_x\sigma_y\rangle_{\Lambda_{Mn},\beta_c}\geq \frac{c_0}{(1\vee|x-y|)^{d-2}}.
\end{equation}

