[Lemma lem:coal-equiv of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] Fix ${\widehat B} \in \widehat{\mathcal{K}}_c$. Then with ${\boldsymbol{\pi}}^{{\widehat B},u,{\raisebox{1.3pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}}$ and ${\boldsymbol{\pi}}^{{\widehat B},v,{\raisebox{1.3pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}}$ defined as in Lemma (lm:xBhatproc of the paper), for $\mathbb{P}$-almost every $\omega$, for any $u,v\in\mathbb{Z}^2$, and for all coalescing pairs $(\pi,\gamma)\in\mathcal{G}_u^\omega\times\mathcal{G}_v^\omega$, 
\begin{equation}
\bigl\{s\in[0,1]:{\boldsymbol{\pi}}^{{\widehat B},u,s}(\omega)\preceq \pi\bigr\} = \bigl\{s\in[0,1]:{\boldsymbol{\pi}}^{{\widehat B},v,s}(\omega)\preceq \gamma\bigr\}.\qedhere
\end{equation}

