[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2604.13819, 'Convolution, cumulants and infinitesimal generators in the formal power series ring'] If $\{Q_s\}_{s\ge 0} \subset  \mathcal{A}_{r}^{(t)}$ satisfies that 
\begin{itemize}
\item $Q_0=1$;
\item $Q_{s_1} \boxplus^t Q_{s_2} = Q_{s_1+s_2}$ for all $s_1,s_2\ge0$;
\item $\|Q_s- 1\|_{r}^{(t)} \to 0$ as $s\to 0^+$.
\end{itemize}
then $\{T_{Q_s}\}_{s\ge0}$ is a strongly continuous semigroup.

