[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For $x\in C$, $A\in\calX$ and $k\in\N^d$,

\begin{equation*}
\psi_k(x,A)=\psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\psi_{k-r}(y,A).
\end{equation*}

Consequently,

\begin{equation*}
\Psi_k(x,A)=\Psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\Psi_{k-r}(y,A),
\end{equation*}

where $\Psi^C=s_0*\psi^C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

In the potential outcomes framework (Neyman-Rubin causal model), for each unit $i$ in a population and binary treatment $T_i \in \{0, 1\}$, there exist two potential outcomes: $Y_i(1)$, the outcome if the unit receives treatment ($T_i = 1$), and $Y_i(0)$, the outcome if the unit receives control ($T_i = 0$). The observed outcome is $Y_i = T_i Y_i(1) + (1 - T_i) Y_i(0)$.
Stable Unit Treatment Value Assumption (SUTVA)
Treatment is binary T \in {0, 1}

[Defn 37 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] With notation as above, let $D$ be an $f$-big $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $X$.
We define the numerical vanishing order of $D$ along $v$ as
\begin{equation*}
v_{\num}(D/S)=
\inf_{S^0 \subset S} 
\inf \left\{ v(D') \middle|
\begin{gathered}
 \text{$D'$ is a $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $f^{-1}(S^0)$} \\
 \text{such that $D|_{f^{-1}(S^0)} \equiv_{S^0} D' \geq 0$}
\end{gathered} 
\right\}, 
\end{equation*}
where $S^0$ runs through all open neighborhoods of $c_{X}(v)$ in $S$.
By definition, $v_{\num}(D/S)$ only depends on the $f$-numerical equivalence class of $D$.

