[Proposition prop:ap1:superposition of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $f:[0, T] \times \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m$ satisfies a linear growth condition. Suppose $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}

    \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} |x|^2 \mu_0(dx) < \infty.
\end{equation}
Then, the trajectory $\{\mu_t\}_{t \in [0, T]}$ is a weak solution to (equation eq:ap1:formalPDE of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def:ap1:wp of the paper) if and only if there is a weak solution $\tilde{\mu} \in \mathcal{P}(C[0, T]; \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m))$ to the following SDE
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    dX(t) &= - f\big(t, X(t)\big) dt + \sqrt{2}dW_t,
    X(0) &\sim \mu_0
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
such that $\mu_t = \tilde{\mu}_t$ for all $t \in [0, T]$.

