[Theorem thm : MAIN of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Assume~(equation ass : Intro/main_thm/SubcriticalAtom of the paper) and~(equation ass : Intro/main_thm/exp_moment of the paper). The process $\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( \SPT \aftergroup\egroup\originalright)_{n\ge 1}$ follows the large deviation principle at speed $n$ with the good rate function
    \begin{align}
        \notag \FdT : \mathcal F_{\mathrm b}  &\longrightarrow \intervalleff0\infty \\
        D &\longmapsto
        \begin{cases}
            \FdTmon(D) &\text{ if } D \in \RegPD[\mu],\\
            \infty &\text{ otherwise.}
        \end{cases}
    \end{align}
    In other words, for all $A\in \mathcal{B}\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( \mathcal F_{\mathrm b}  \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) $,
    \begin{equation}

        \inf_{D\in \overline{A}} \FdT(D) \le 
        \liminf_{n\to\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log\Pb{\SPT \in A} \le 
        \limsup_{n\to\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log\Pb{\SPT \in A} \le 
        \inf_{D\in \mathring{A}} \FdT(D).
   \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

