body:
[Lemma TISGM-to-cavity of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Given any $\pmb\rho\in \TISGM^{\psi,\bar\psi}_{T^{\k}}$, its boundary law $\ell\in \P(\X)$ is a fixed point of the recursion $\BP:\P(\X)\rightarrow \P(\X)$ defined by
    \begin{align}
        \BP\ell(x)=\frac{1}{\zeta}\bar\psi(x)\cpr{\sum_{z\in \X}\psi(x,z)\ell(z)}^{\k-1},\quad \forall x\in \X,
    \end{align}
    where $\zeta$ is the normalizing constant. In fact, there is a one-one correspondence between the set $\TISGM^{\psi,\bar\psi}_{T^\k}$ and the set of fixed points $\Delta^*\coloneqq\pr{\ell\in \P(\X): \BP\ell=\ell}$. 
    Moreover, for any $\ell\in \Delta^*$, the edge marginal $\pi_{\pmb \rho_1}$ of the TISGM $\pmb \rho$ corresponding to $\ell$ satisfies  
    \begin{align}
        \pi_{\pmb\rho_1}(x,z)\propto \ell(x)\psi(x,z)\ell(z),\quad \forall x,z\in \X.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 3 (Wirtinger test) of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $g\in L^2(\mathbb R)$ be nonzero. Define
\begin{equation}
    \delta_g:= \frac{1}{2} \inf_{x\in[0,1]}
    \sqrt{\frac{\displaystyle\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z}|\widehat g((x-k))|^2}{\displaystyle\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z}(x-k)^2|\widehat g((x-k))|^2}}.
\end{equation}
Then, the Gabor system $\mathcal{G}(g,\delta \mathbb Z\times \mathbb Z)$ is a frame for $L^2(\mathbb R)$ for all $\delta < \delta_g$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

