body:
[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Assume the linear growth condition \eqref{LG-condition-existence}. Suppose $X = (X(t))_{t \in [0,T]}$ is a solution to equation \eqref{path_dependent_sde_existence}
    with initial condition $X(0)$ being $\ccF_0$-measurable and satisfying $E[\|X(0)\|^{2m}] < \infty$ for some $m \geq 1$. Then,
    \begin{equation}
        E\left[\sup_{t \in [0,T]} \|X(t)\|^{2m}\right] \leq (1+3E[\|X(0)\|^{2m}])e^{3C_{LG}T(T+4)}.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, $X$ satisfies $E[\int_{0}^{T} \|X(s)\|^{2m} dt] < \infty$.

