body:
[Lemma lem_not_too_dense of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Assume (equation p_upper of the paper) and (equation p_lower of the paper).
For every $\epsilon>0$ and $\delta>0$, there exists $\eta = \eta(\epsilon,\delta,\mathfrak{C}/\mathfrak{c})>0$ small enough that
\begin{subequations} 
\begin{align} 

\sup_{a\in[0,1]}\mathbb{P}\Big(\parbox{0.36\textwidth}{\centering $\mathcal{S}_n$ is a convex chain such that \\ $\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([a,a+\eta]\times[0,1])\big)\geqslant \delta n$}\Big)
&\leqslant \epsilon^n\cdot \mathbb{P}(\text{$\mathcal{S}_n$ is a convex chain}) \\

\text{and} \quad
\sup_{a\in[0,1]}\mathbb{P}\Big(\parbox{0.36\textwidth}{\centering $\mathcal{S}_n$ is a convex chain such that \\ $\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([0,1]\times[a,a+\eta])\big)\geqslant \delta n$}\Big)
&\leqslant \epsilon^n\cdot \mathbb{P}(\text{$\mathcal{S}_n$ is a convex chain})
\end{align}
\end{subequations}
for all sufficiently large $n$.
In particular, for all large $n$ we have
\eq{
\mathbb{P}(\text{$\mathcal{S}_n$ is an $(\eta,\delta)$-bad convex chain})
\leqslant 2\epsilon^n\cdot\mathbb{P}(\text{$\mathcal{S}_n$ is a convex chain}).
}

