[Prop prop_no_g2 of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] There exists a consistent APS $S$ satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathsf{E}_S(\triangle)$ holds for every one-variable APS term $\triangle v$ of degree three.
    \item For every one-variable APS term $\triangle v$ of odd degree, $\triangle\top$ is refutable in $S$.
\end{enumerate}

