body:
[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t\in T}$ be a centered Gaussian process with a finite index set $T$.
Then we have
\begin{align*}
  \Ex X_{\uptau_{\beta,\mu}} \gtrsim \int_0^\Delta 
  \sqrt{R_{\overline{\sm}_{\beta,\mu}}(\epsilon^2)\wedge I(X;\uptau_{\beta,\mu})} \dif \epsilon .
\end{align*}

[Lemma restr-equiv-rQ of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be a continuous group homomorphism, and let ${\mathcal{F}},{\mathcal{F}}'$ be collections of closed subgroups of $G$ and $G'$, respectively, such that $\alpha(H)\in{\mathcal{F}}'$ for every $H\in{\mathcal{F}}$. Then 
    \[
        \alpha_!\colon\textbf{\textup{$\bm G$-Top}}\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G'}$-Top}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
\alpha^*
    \]
    is a Quillen adjunction with homotopical right adjoint for the ${\mathcal{F}}$-model structure on the left and the ${\mathcal{F}}'$-model structure on the target.
    \begin{proof}
        Note that we have an equality of functors $(-)^H\circ\alpha^*=(-)^{\alpha(H)}$. Thus, it follows immediately from the definitions that $\alpha^*$ preserves weak equivalences and fibrations.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

