[Lemma lem: adding external field in sle continuity of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $\mathcal{F}_i$ be the
$\sigma$-algebra generated by $H^i$.

There exists a constant $c_3>0$  

such that for any $1\le i\le n$, we have \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb{P}}\Big(\max\{|\mathsf{a}_i|,|\mathsf{a}_i^+|,|\mathsf{a}_i^-|\}\ge \frac{1}{2}\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\Big)\le c_3^{-1}\exp\Big(-c_3\big({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}}\big)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\Big).
\end{equation}
In addition, we have \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb{E}}\Big(\max\{|\mathsf{a}_i|,|\mathsf{a}_i^+|,|\mathsf{a}_i^-|\}\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\Big)\le 1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

