body:
[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $b > 0$, $\vec{y} \in \weyl_2$, and let $f,g \in C([0,b])$ be such that $f(b) > y_1 > y_2 > g(b)$. Then 
\begin{align}
&\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{pin}}^{b, \vec{y}}\left( \mathcal{Q}_2(t) \geq g(t) \mbox{ for all $t \in [0,b]$ and } \min_{s \in [0,b]} |\mathcal{Q}_2(s)- g(s)| = 0   \right) = 0,  \\
&\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{pin}}^{b, \vec{y}}\left( \mathcal{Q}_1(t) \leq f(t) \mbox{ for all $t \in [0,b]$ and } \min_{s \in [0,b]} |\mathcal{Q}_1(s)- f(s)| = 0   \right) = 0. 
\end{align}

