{"artifact_digest":"sha256:984fce51814e885433e655e5e825493986f934b02d2184f161410d295e3854e9","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/98/984fce51814e885433e655e5e825493986f934b02d2184f161410d295e3854e9.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:851c2716eb67a70c69c90b293ee31ed585711362db170224489def809d96c48d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-27520-lemma-12-single-loop-to-boundary","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_059","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_059.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-27520-lemma-12-single-loop-to-boundary","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Write $K_r$ for the matrix with $K_r(x,y) = \tau^{d(x,y)}_\kappa$ for $x,y \in \partial B(r)$, and let $\mathbf{1}_r$ be the vector with $| \partial B(r)|$ many ones. Lemmas~\ref{l:greens_f} and \ref{L:loop_det} give that
    \begin{align*}
         \mu_\kappa(\ell : 0 \in \ell, \ell \cap \partial B(r) \neq \emptyset) &=  \mu_\kappa(\ell : 0 \in \ell) +  \mu_\kappa(\ell :  \ell \cap \partial B(r) \neq \emptyset) \\
         &\hspace{2cm}-  \mu_\kappa(\ell :  \ell \cap (\partial B(r) \cup \{0\}) \neq \emptyset) \\
