[Lemma le:tightness_bdry_single_loop of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] There exists $\zeta > 0$ such that the following is true. Fix $0 < r < 1$ and $c_1 > 0$. For $\delta > 0$, let $E_\delta$ be the event that there exists a loop $\mathcal {L} \in \Gamma$ and two non-overlapping segments $\ell_1,\ell_2 \subseteq \mathcal {L}$ such that the left boundaries of $\ell_1,\ell_2$ intersect and there are four points $\widehat{x},x,y,\widehat{y}$ on their intersection in exactly this order such that
\begin{itemize}
\item $\abs{x-\widehat{x}} \ge \delta^{c_1}$, $\abs{y-\widehat{y}} \ge \delta^{c_1}$,
\item if $U_{x,y}$ is the region bounded between the left boundaries of $\ell_1,\ell_2$ from $x$ to $y$, then $U_{x,y} \subseteq B(0,r)$, $\mathrm{diam}(U_{x,y}) \le \delta$, and $D_\epsilon^{\partial U_{x,y}} \ge \delta^\zeta+\epsilon^{a_0}$.
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[E_\delta] = o^\infty(\delta)$.

[Lemma of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Let $K \subset \{\lvert z \lvert >1\}$ a compact. Then there exists $C_K>0$ such that almost surely \begin{equation*}
        \sup_{z\in K}\lvert \lvert \mathbf{R}_{N}(z) \lvert \lvert \leq C_K
    \end{equation*} 
    for all sufficiently large $N$.

