[Lemma lem:quadratic-stability of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] For $\beta\in(0,1)$ and $s>0$, all matrices $A_\lambda(s,\beta)$, $\lambda\in[1,\kappa]$, are Schur stable, meaning that their spectral radii are strictly less than one, if and only if
\begin{equation}
 0<s<\frac{2(1+\beta)}{\kappa}.
\end{equation}
For OBABO, using $s=h^2(1+\beta)/2$, this is equivalent to $0<h<2/\sqrt\kappa$. Moreover, if $h\ge2/\sqrt\kappa$, the OBABO chain for the potential $U_\kappa(x)=\kappa\lvert x\rvert^2/2$ has no invariant probability law.

