[Lemma lem:zero_boundary_conditions of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Fix $j \in \{1,\ldots,N\}$ such that
	\begin{align*}
		\partial U_j  \subseteq \overline{\bigcup_{\SCL \in \Gamma_A^{\mathrm{out}} \cup \Gamma_A^{\mathrm{in}} \cup \Gamma_A} \SCL}
	\end{align*}
	and such that $\partial U_j$ contains a crossing of $A$ made by a loop of $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{\pm \lambda\}$. If the boundary conditions of the field $\Psi|_{U_j}$ on $\partial U_j$ are not given by the zero function, then we have that $U_j$ is contained in the region enclosed by an outermost loop in $\overline{\Gamma}$.

