[Lemma 18 (Lipschitz regularity of Parisi functional) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] There is a constant $C>0$ such that, for every $t, t' \ge 0$, $p,p' \in \mcl Q_{\infty, \le \lambda_\infty}^\sS$, and $q,q' \in \mcl Q_1^\sS$, we have
\begin{gather*}
    \Ll|\sP_{t,q}(p)-\sP_{t',q'}(p')\Rr|\leq C\Ll(\Ll|t-t'\Rr|+\Ll|p-p'\Rr|_{L^1}+\Ll|q-q'\Rr|_{L^1}\Rr),
    \\
    \Ll|\partial_q\psi\Ll(q+t\nabla\xi(p)\Rr)-\partial_q\psi\Ll(q'+t'\nabla\xi(p')\Rr)\Rr|_{L^1}\leq C\Ll(\Ll|t-t'\Rr|+\Ll|p-p'\Rr|_{L^1}+\Ll|q-q'\Rr|_{L^1}\Rr).
\end{gather*}

