[Prop 64 (Bulk mixing) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] The following holds if the constant $L$ in \Cref{def:bulkcells} is large enough. Fix real numbers $q \ge \overline{q}$ and a point $z_0 \in \mathfrak{L}_{q}$ satisfying \eqref{eq:distanzabis} and  
\begin{flalign}

	0 \le q - \overline{q} < N^{5A\delta/4-1} (\mathfrak{d}_{z_0} \mathfrak{e}_{z_0;q})^{-1/2}.
\end{flalign}

\noindent Further assume that $H_0 (z) \le
        \mathcal{H}_{q} (z)+N^{\delta-1}$ for each $z \in 
        \mathfrak{Y}$. 
        Under the Glauber dynamics restricted to $\mathfrak Y$, with the ceiling constraint $\cH_q+N^{\delta-1}$ on $\mathfrak{Y}$, 
        we have w.o.p. 
        \begin{eqnarray}

H_t (z) \le \mathcal{H}_{\bar q} (z),  
        \end{eqnarray}
        for all
        \begin{equation}

          z\in \mathfrak{Y}^-,\qquad t \in[\mathtt t,N^{5}
            ],  \quad \mathtt t:= q^{-1} N^{1+6 A\delta}(\md_{z_0}\me_{z_0;q})^{-1/2}.
        \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

