[Theorem theorem3.2 of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] [[MR131894]]
    Fix $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and consider $\xi_1,\cdots,\xi_k$ independent random variables. Fix real numbers $h_1,\cdots,h_k>0$. Then given any $h\geq \max_{j=1,\cdots,k}h_j$,
    $$
\mathcal{Q}(\sum_{j=1}^k\xi_j,h)\leq C_{(equation theorem3.2 of the paper)}h\left(\sum_{j=1}^k(1-\mathcal{Q}(\xi_j,h_j))h_j^2\right)^{-1/2}
    $$
    for a universal constant $C_{(equation theorem3.2 of the paper)}>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:covariance_inequality of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] For each $m\geqslant 2$, there exists a constant $C_m$ such that if  $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, $\left(X_i\right)_{i\in\mathbb Z}$ is a strictly stationary sequence taking   $h\colon S^m\to \mathbb R$ is a canonical kernel such that $\sup_{x_1,\dots,x_m\in S}\left|h\left(x_1,\dots,x_m\right)\right|\leqslant R$ and $N\geqslant m$, then 
 \begin{align}
     \E{\pr{U_{m,N+a}\left(h\right)-U_{m,a}\left(h\right)}^2}&
     \leqslant C_{m} \left(N+a\right)^{ m-1 } N\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^{N+a}k^{m-1} 
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2,\\
     \E{\max_{m\leqslant n\leqslant N}\pr{U_{m,n}\left(h\right)   }^2    }
     &\leqslant C_mN^{m }\left(\log  N\right)^2\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^Nk^{m-1}
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2.
 \end{align}

