[Thm 11 of arXiv:2506.18834, '\large\bf On the random-time and finite-time ruin probability for widely dependent claim s'] In a nonstandard renewal risk model,
let $Z_i,\ i\ge1$ be WLOD random variables with dominating coefficients $g_{L,H}(n),\ n\ge1$.
If
\begin{eqnarray}
g_{L,H}(n)=o(e^{an})\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \text{for some }\ \ a>0,\ \ \ \text{as}\ \ \ n\to\infty,
\end{eqnarray}
then for each $\delta>0$, there exists $r=r(H)>0$ such that
\begin{eqnarray}
Ee^{rN(t)}\textbf{\emph{1}}_{\{N(t)>(1+\delta)\mu_H^{-1}t\}}\to0,\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \text{as}\ \ \ t\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

