[Lemm 7 (Theorem 2.3 in \cite{Yong:20}) of arXiv:2506.10213, 'Coupling of forward-backward stochastic differential equations on the Wiener space, and ap'] Assume Assumption \ref{coefficient:assume:general}. For some $p\in[2,\infty)$, if
\begin{equation}
    \begin{cases}
        (\overline{K}_p)^{1/p}\left(\dfrac{p}{p-1} + 2(\underline{K}_p)^{-1/p}\dfrac{2p-1}{p-1}\right)L_g L_{\mu,3} < 1, & \text{if } p\in (2,\infty),\\[1mm]
        L_g L_{\mu,3} < 1, & \text{if } p=2,
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}
then there exists a constant \(\delta > 0\), depending on all the Lipschitz constants, such that if \(T-t\le \delta\), the FBSDE \eqref{fbsde:equ:general} admits a unique solution \(\Tz=(X,Y,Z)\) in \(\cL^p\)
where $X$ and $Y$ are continuous processes and $Z$ is predictable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

