[Lem exp_c_k_star of arXiv:2606.15339, 'Uniform integrability of the distance to the nearest leaf in random trees'] Let $(\mathcal{T}_n)_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of size-conditioned simply generated trees of type~I or~II, with $0<p_0<1$. Then
	\begin{align}
		c_k^{*}=\mathbf{P}(\partial(\mathcal{T}^{*})\geq k)\leq (1-p_0)^{\,k}\,,\qquad k\geq1\,.
	\end{align}
	In particular, $\partial(\mathcal{T}^{*})$ has finite moments of all orders.

