body:
[Lemma 137 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $u,f,f_{i}$,
$i=1,...,d$, be  
function on $\bR^{d+1}$ of class $L_{1,\loc}$
such that (in the sense of generalized functions)
\begin{equation}

\text{either}\quad
\partial_{t}u=f+D_{i}f_{i},\quad\text{or}
\quad u\geq0\quad\text{and}\quad 
\partial_{t}u\leq f+D_{i}f_{i}.
\end{equation}
Let $q\in(2,d+2]$, $\rho\in(0,\infty)$,
\index{$S$@Miscelenea!$\bar b_{R}$@$\hat b_{q,\rho}$}
and
$$
\hat b_{q,\rho}:=\sup_{r\leq\rho}r\sup_{C\in\bC_{r}}\dashnorm b\|_{L_{q}(C)}<\infty.
$$
Let $C\in \bC_{\rho }$ and let $\zeta\in C^{\infty}_{0}(C)$
be a nonnegative functions with the integral
of its square equal to one.
Then  
$$
\int_{\bR^{d+1}}b^{2}\zeta^{2}u^{2}\,dxdt
\leq N\hat b_{q,\rho }
 \int_{\bR^{d+1}}  \zeta^{2} |Du|^{2}
\,dxdt
$$
\begin{equation}

+N\hat b_{q,\rho }\rho ^{-d-4}
\int_{\bR^{d+1}}u^{2}I_{C}\,dxdt
+N\hat b_{q,\rho }\rho ^{-d-2}
\int_{\bR^{d+1}}I_{C} \big[\rho ^{2} f^{2}  +\sum_{i}f_{i}^{2}\big]\,dxdt,
\end{equation}
where the constants $N$ depend only on $d,q$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

