[Cor 5 of arXiv:2605.27974, 'Discrete approximation of semi-Dirichlet forms with non-symmetric perturbations of resista'] Assume that $\mathscr{C}_{\infty}=\mathscr{X}_{\infty}$. Then, 
$\{ u_{n} \}_{n \in \N} \,(u_{n} \in \mathscr{X}_{n})$ strongly converges to $u \in \mathscr{X}_{\infty}$ 
if and only if $\limtoinfty{n} \norm{\Phi_{n}u-u_{n}}_{\mathscr{X}_{n}}=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:price-equality-minimax of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and $X:\Omega\to{\mathbb{R}\cup\{\infty\}}$ measurable.
  Then $\overline{\mathbb{E}} X = \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$ if and only if
  \begin{equation}
    \sup_{P\in\Delta(\Omega)} \inf_{Z\in\mathrm{mdcl}(\mathcal{Z})} \mathbb{E}_P [X-Z] = \inf_{Z\in\mathrm{mdcl}(\mathcal{Z})} \sup_{P\in\Delta(\Omega)} \mathbb{E}_P[X-Z]~.
  \end{equation}

