[Lemma Lem: identical sequence of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Assume that $\{X_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ is a $d$-dimensional identical sequence on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$. Set 
		\begin{equation*}
			S_{n,0}=0, \ S_{n,m}=\frac{X_1+\cdots+X_m}{n}, \ m\geq 1,
		\end{equation*}
		Let $Z\stackrel{d}{=} X_1$ and $v^Z_n$ be defined by (equation 1225-2 of the paper)-(equation 1225-3 of the paper) with $v^Z_n(0,x)=\phi(x)$ for some $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. Then we have
		\begin{equation}
	\Big|v^Z_n\bigl(1,0)-\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\phi(S_{n,n})]\Big|\le \sum_{k=1}^{n}\Big|\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Bigl[v^Z_n(\frac{n-k}{n},S_{n,k})\Bigr]-\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Bigl[\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Bigl[v^Z_n(\frac{n-k}{n},x+\frac{X_{k}}{n})\Bigr]\Big|_{x=S_{n,k-1}}\Bigr]\Big|.
		\end{equation}

