[Cor fass1-and-fass2-are-satisfied of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Under (fass1 of the paper), (as-W of the paper) and (as-U of the paper) hold with $W, W', U, U'$ as in (func-WU of the paper) and \begin{equation}
    V(\phi) \coloneqq \sum_{i=1}^n \rho_i V_i(x_i) \,,
\end{equation}
where $\rho_i > 0$, $x \coloneqq \phi(0)$, and $V_i: (0,\infty) \to [0,\infty)$ is a smooth function such that 
\begin{equation}
    V_i(x) = \begin{cases}
        -\ln(x) & x \in (0, 1)\,, \\
        0 & x \geq 2 \,.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}

[Theorem MainThm: infinite_l_activation_time of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \ge 2$. Assume $Q$ is a symmetric, translation-invariant, and heavy-tailed transition kernel on $\mathbb Z^d$ with exponent $\alpha > 0$, and let $Q_L$ be its standard projection onto $\mathbb{T}^d_L$. Consider the frog model on $\mathbb{T}^d_L$ equipped with $Q_L$. 
Assume that all particles have infinite lifespan. 
\begin{enumerate}[left=0.3cm]
\item If $\alpha \in (0, d)$, then for any $\lambda > 0$ and $\varepsilon > 0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{L \rightarrow \infty} \mathbb P_L^+\left(\mathcal{A}((\log L)^{\Delta + \varepsilon}) = \mathbb{T}^d_L\right) = 1.
    \end{align*}
\item If $\alpha \ge d$, then for any $\lambda > 0$, there exists a positive constant $C$ such that
\begin{align*}
\lim_{L \rightarrow \infty} \mathbb P_L^+\left(\mathcal{A}(C L) = \mathbb{T}^d_L\right) = 1.
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 18 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For every $a > 0$, with $K_a \coloneqq \log\left(e^{1/(2a^2)} - 1\right)$,
\begin{align*}
    (1-p)\,\nu_{\max}(p,a) = a\left(\log\frac1p + K_a + o(1)\right)
    \qquad (p \downarrow 0),
\end{align*}
and consequently $R(p,a) \to a$ as $p \downarrow 0$; in particular $c^{\SE}(1,a) \ge a$.

