[Proposition prop:coupling_valid_epssqrtn of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] Assume all the conditions of Proposition (prop:connection_under_truncation of the paper). Consider the restricted exploration process $A_c(o_1,t)$ and its coupling with the breadth-first exploration process $\mathcal T_n(t)$ in $\mathcal T_n$ as in Lemma (lem:rest_coupling of the paper), and the stopping time $\tau$ as in (equation eq:stop_time_rest_coupconf of the paper). Then 
    \begin{align*}
        \liminf_{n \to \infty}\Prob{\tau\leq \epsilon \sqrt{n}}=O(\epsilon^2),
    \end{align*}
    where the $O(\cdot)$ term on the right-hand side above is as $\epsilon\to 0$.

