[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] We consider $1 \le d \le N^{\delta/4}$ with $0<\delta < 1/3$. There exists a constant $C>0$ such that if $m \in \N$ satisfies $m \le  C^{-1} \sqrt{d} \log N$ and $\nu>0$ then 
    \begin{align*}
    \|X^m \| &\le C N^{ (\nu+1)/2} m^2 \sqrt{d}
    \end{align*}
    with probability at least $1 - N^{- \nu}$.

