body:
[Proposition prop:Ergodic:Fredholm of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Let $\nu\in C^{2,\alpha}_p(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be the strictly positive density of the unique invariant measure of $(\dot{Z}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ on the torus, and $f\in C^{0,\alpha}_p(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be such that $\nu(f)=0$. Then, there exists a unique $\eta^f\in C_p^{2,\alpha}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ that satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathcal{L} \eta^f = f,
    \end{equation*}
    and such that $\nu(\eta^f)=0$.
    Furthermore, there exists a positive constant $C=C(d,\|\sigma\|_{0,\alpha}, \|b\|_{0,\alpha})$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \|\eta^f\|_{2,\alpha} \leq C\|f\|_{0,\alpha}.
    \end{equation}

