[Lem Lemma: intertwining sections of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] Up to passing to a finite extension of $X$, there is a measurable map $\sigma: \mathbb{Z}^d \times X \to \Gamma_0$ satisfying:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item for every $x \in X$, the map $t \mapsto \sigma(t, x)$ is a section of the projection $p: \Gamma_0 \to \mathbb{Z}^d$;
        \item for every $x \in X$, $t \in \mathbb{Z}^d$, and $t' \in \Gamma$, $\sigma(t + p(t'), x) = \sigma(t, x) \cdot t'$;
        \item for every $\gamma \in \SL_d(\mathbb{Z})$, $t \in \mathbb{Z}^d$, and $\nu$-a.e.\ $x \in X$, $\alpha(\gamma, x)(\sigma(t, x)) = \sigma(\gamma(t), \gamma \cdot x)$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Thm cokernel distribution theorem 1 of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Let $G$ be a finite abelian group and $\mathcal{P}$ be a finite set of primes including those dividing $|G|$. 
Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for every prime $p$ in $\mathcal{P}$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item if $2 \in \mathcal{P}$, then for every $\delta>0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
$$
\lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong G\right) = \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G)|}\prod_{p\in \mathcal{P}} \prod_{i=1}^\infty (1-p^{-i})
= \prod_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 14 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] For every $\delta \in (0,1)$ and $\varepsilon > 0$, 
