[Lemma lem:apply-bar-main-quadratic of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the modified $GI/GI/n$\xspace system satisfying Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable of the paper), with the load $\rho < 1$. We have
    \begin{equation}

        (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{Q}
        =  \frac{\rho\textnormal{Var}\left[\Lambda A\right] + \textnormal{Var}\left[\mu S\right] + 1-\rho}{2} +  \sum_{j=1}^n \Gamma_{{s,j}}  - \Gamma_a \;, 
    \end{equation}
    where $\Gamma_{{s,j}}$ and $\Gamma_{a}$ are defined as: 
    \begin{align}

        \Gamma_{{s,j}} &= \Ep{s}{\vmathbb{1}{\left\{Q=0\right\}} \mu R_{{s,j}}} - (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{\mu R_{{s,j}}} \quad \forall j\in [n]\\

        \Gamma_{a} &= \Ep{s}{\vmathbb{1}{\left\{Q=0\right\}} \Lambda R_a} - (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{\Lambda R_{a}},
    \end{align}
    and $\Ep{s}{\cdot} \triangleq \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \Ep{{s,i}}{\cdot}$ is the Palm expectation with respect to all completion events. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Suppose that the assumptions of Theorem \ref{thmGS} are satisfied, and let $\Xi(t)$, $t\in \RR$, be defined as in \eqref{next-jump}. Then the process $(Y^+(t), \Xi(t))$, $t \geq 0$, is a time-homogeneous Markov process, under all $\PP^{(x,s)}$, $(x,s)\in \RR^d\times (-\infty,0]$, and the filtration $\mathcal{G}_t$, $t \geq0$, generated by $N(s), S_0, \dots, {S_{N(s)+1}}, T_0, \dots, {T_{N(s)+1}}$, $s \leq t$. Its semigroup $\wt P_t^+$, $t \geq 0$, satisfies for $(x,s)\in \RR^d\times (0,+\infty)$
		\begin{align}
			\wt P^+_tf(x,s)&=\mathds{1}_{[0\le t<s]}f(x,s-t)+\mathds{1}_{[0<s\le t ]}\int_{\RR^d}\int_{(0,+\infty)}\wt P^+_{t-s}f(y,w)\mu_{x}(dy,dw),
		\end{align}
		for any function $f \in \mathcal{B}_b (\mathbb{R}^d \times (0, +\infty))$.

