[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $\hat \tau\in \hat{\mathcal T}^F$. Let $M\in \mathcal M$ be a minimal class. The following properties are satisfied:
\begin{itemize}	
\item[i)] $\hat\tau$ contains no edges going out from $M$, if $\hat \tau$ is rooted inside $M$;
\item[ii)] $\hat\tau$ contains only one edge (necessarily slow) going out from $M$, if $\hat \tau$ is not rooted inside $M$;
\item[iii)] $\hat \tau$ contains no slow edges connecting two vertices of $M$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

