body:
[Theorem th:um:SPDE of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Suppose $2H\alpha =3$. Fix a compact rectangle $I\times J \subset (0\,,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}$, $t_0 > 0$ and $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}$.
Then, a.s.,
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{x,y \in J: 0<|x-y|\le h} \frac{|u(t_0\,,x)-u(t_0\,,y)|}{|x-y|\log(1/|x-y|)} = K_3,
\end{align}
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{t,s\in I: 0<|t-s| \le h} \frac{|u(t\,,x_0)-u(s\,,x_0)|}{|t-s|^{1/\alpha}\sqrt{\log(1/|t-s|)}} = K_4,
\end{align}
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{z,z'\in I\times J: 0<\phi(z,z') \le h} \frac{|u(z)-u(z')|}{\phi(z\,,z')\sqrt{\log(1/\phi(z\,,z'))}} = K_5,
\end{align}
for some non-random numbers $K_3, K_4, K_5 \in (0\,,\infty)$ that may depend on $I, J$ or $t_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:area-odd of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For
\begin{equation}
A^{ij}(X)=\frac12\left(\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(X)}{ij}-\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(X)}{ji}\right),
\end{equation}
one has
\begin{equation}
A^{ij}(\overleftarrow X)=-A^{ij}(X).
\end{equation}
Hence for a process whose time reversal exchanges the excitation roles, the expected cross-area changes sign, as in the reversal experiment of (sec:numerics of the paper).

