[Corollary 26 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $T=\E X$ and $X$ be a random variable with density $f$ with respect to $\pi_{T}.$ Assume that $f$ is bounded away from zero and infinity and $H(X|\pi_{T}) < \infty.$ Then, for every $a$ in $[0,1],$ we have
    \begin{displaymath}
        \frac{d}{da} \big(  H  ( T_{a}(X) | \pi_{aT} ) \big) = T H \big( T_{a} (S(X)) | T_{a}(X) \big) .
    \end{displaymath}

