body:
[Corollary High Probability Overlap Bounds of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For all $t \leq t_*$ and edge indices $i$ with $|\lambda_i - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}$:
\begin{equation}
|X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)| \prec N^{1/6+\varepsilon}
\end{equation}
while for bulk indices with $|\lambda_i - 2| \geq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}$:
\begin{equation}
|X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)| \prec N^{\varepsilon}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

