body:
[Lemma l5.1 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] For any $x,y\in \mathbb{Z}^+$ there exist random processes $\tilde{\xi}(t)$ and $\hat{\xi}(t)$
such that $\tilde{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_x(t)$, $\hat{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_y(t)$, and the following equality holds
\begin{equation} 
 \mathbf{P}\left(\sup\limits_{t\geq 0}|\tilde{\xi}(t)-\hat{\xi}(t)|\leq|x-y|\right)=1.
\end{equation}

