[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.06317, 'Sharp Tail Bounds Beyond Twice the Mean'] Let $w\ge 0$ and $0\le m\le \min\{1,w\}$ and denote the remaining budget $r=w-m$. Let $x>1$ as well as $z\in [u_0,x)$. Then 
    \begin{equation}
    \frac{m}{z}\min\left\{1,\frac{r}{x-z}\right\} +\left(1-\frac{m}{z}\right) P(x,z,r)\le P(x,z,w).
    \end{equation}

