[Defn 1 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume \ref{H0}--\ref{H3} hold. We say that $(\Omega,\mathcal F,(\mathcal F_t)_{t\geq0},\mathbb P, W,X)$ is a weak mild solution to \eqref{abstract_formulation} if $(\Omega,\mathcal F,(\mathcal F_t)_{t\geq0},\mathbb P)$ is a complete filtered probability space, $X=\{X(t)\}_{t\in[0,T]}$ is a continuous $(\mathcal F_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$-adapted $H$-valued process and $W=(W(t))_{t\geq0}$ is a $U$-valued cylindrical Wiener process such that, for every $t\in[0,T]$,
\begin{align}

X(t)=e^{tA}x+\int_0^te^{(t-s)A}\mathcal VC(s,X(s))ds+\int_0^t e^{(t-s)A}\mathcal GdW(s), \qquad \mathbb P\textrm{-a.s.}    
