body:
[Lemma 12 (Global 3G inequality) of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] Suppose $G(x,y)$ is the global Green function of a geometric stable process on $\mathbb{R}^d$.
    Then there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that for all $x, y, z \in \mathbb{R}^d$,
    \begin{align}

      \frac{G(x,y)G(y,z)}{G(x,z)} \le C \left( G(x,y) + G(y,z) \right).
    \end{align}

