[Definition def:gamma:summing of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] An operator \( A \in \mathcal{L}(H,X) \) is \emph{\( \gamma \)-summing} if
    \begin{equation} 
        \sup_{(h_k)_{k=1}^n \in \mathcal{F}(H)} \int_\Omega \left\| \sum_{k=1}^n \xi_k(\omega) A h_k \right\|^2 \mu(d\omega) < \infty.
    \end{equation}

[Proposition McNeiletal of arXiv:2605.20471, 'Note on the Weak Convergence of Hyperplane $α$-Quantile Functionals and Their Continuity i'] {(see e.g. [McNeiletal]; A.3. p. 641-642)}

	If $x=(x_t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}$ is $\mathbb{R}$-valued nondecreasing, not necessarily càdlàg, then the generalized inverse given by $x^{-1}(y):=\inf\{t:x_t\geq y\}$ is such that:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $x^{-1}$ is nondecreasing, left-continuous;
		\item $x$ is continuous if and only if $x^{-1}$ is strictly increasing;
		\item $x$ is strictly increasing if and only if $x^{-1}$ is continuous.
	\end{enumerate}

	If $x$ is also right-continuous it follows that $x_t \geq y\iff x^{-1}(y)\leq t$ (equivalently $x_t < y\iff x^{-1}(y)> t$). In fact, right-continuity is needed only for the implication $(\Leftarrow)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary coro: levy1 bounded support of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Fix $S\subseteq\mathbb R$ and let  $X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be an $S$-valued Lévy process with characteristics $(b,a,F)$. Assume that $F$ has bounded support and set
 \begin{align*}
    \mathcal{V}&:=\{h\in H(\mathbb C)\colon |h|_\mathbb R|,|h'|_\mathbb R|,|h''|_\mathbb R|\leq C\exp(a|\cdot|)\text{ for some }a\in \mathbb R, C>0 \}\\
    \mathcal V^*&:=\{\mathbf{u}\in \mathcal{S}^* \colon h_\mathbf{u}=h,  \ h\in \mathcal{V}\}.
\end{align*}
The following conditions hold true.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is an $S$-valued $\mathcal V$-holomorphic process.
    \item  The process $N^h$ given in equation (equation eq:localmart of the paper) is a true martingale for each $h\in \mathcal V$.
    \item  
    Fix $\mathbf{u}\in \mathcal V^*$. Assume that 

        $\int_\mathbb R |h_\mathbf{u}(x)|dx<\infty $ or $ \int_\mathbb R |h_\mathbf{u}(x)|^2 dx<\infty$ and  
     the map $\hat h_\mathbf{u}:\mathbb R\to\mathbb C$ given by 
        \begin{equation}
    \hat h_\mathbf{u}(u):=\int_\mathbb R h_\mathbf{u}(x)e^{-iux}dx
    \end{equation}
 satisfies
\begin{align}
        \int_\mathbb R \exp(|ux|)|\hat{h}_\mathbf{u}(u)|du<\infty,
    \end{align}
    for all $x\in \mathbb R$.  Then there exists a $\mathcal{V}^*$-valued solution $(\mathbf{c}(t))_{t\in[0,T]}$ of (equation eq: ODE pointwise of the paper) with initial condition $\mathbf{u}$ which satisfies condition~(moment formula ii of the paper) and~(moment formula iii of the paper) of Theorem~(th: moment formula holomorphic of the paper). In particular, the holomorphic formula holds true:
    \begin{align*}
    \mathbb E[h_\mathbf{u}(X_T)]=h_{\mathbf{c}(T)}(x_0).
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] Assume the mappings $f_{n}:\R^N\times \R\to\R$, $n\ge 0$, satisfy condition $(f1)$ with a common function $c\in L^{2}(\R^{N}$ and condition $(f2)$ with the same Lipschitz constant $l\in L^{\infty}(\R^{N})$. Suppose that 
\begin{equation}
f_{n}(x,u)\to f_{0}(x,u) \quad \text{ as } \ n\to \infty 
\end{equation}
for a.e. $x\in\R^{N}$ and $u\in\R$. If $F_n: H^1(\R^N)\to L^2(\R^N)$ is the Nemytskii operator determined by $f_{n}$, then, for any $u\in H^{1}(\R^{N})$, 
\begin{align}
F_{n}(u)\to F_{0}(u) \quad \text{in } L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{N}) \text{ as } n\to\infty.
\end{align}
Moreover, for any bounded set $W\subset H^1(\R^N)$, the set $\bigcup_{n\geq 1}F_{n}(W)$ is bounded in $L^2(\R^N)$ and 
\begin{align}   
\beta_{L^{2}}\left(\bigcup_{n\geq 1}F_n(W)\right) \le \hat \varrho (l) \beta_{L^{2}}(W).
\end{align}

