[Proposition 34 (Sobolev, Step 4.d)) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $[\beta]\geq0$ and assume that $\eqref{Pi-_recentre}_\beta$, $\eqref{est_deltaPi-_bounded}_\beta$ and $\eqref{est_deltaPi-_inc}_\beta$ hold,
that $\eqref{est_Gamma}_\beta^\gamma$, $\eqref{est_deltaGamma}_\beta^\gamma$, and $\eqref{est_dGamma}_\beta^\gamma$ hold for all $\gamma$ populated and not purely polynomial, 
and that $\eqref{est_Pi-}_{\beta'}$ and $\eqref{est_deltaPi-}_{\beta'}$ hold for all populated $\beta'\prec\beta$.
Then 

\begin{equation}
\EE^\frac{1}{q} \left|
\delta\Pi_{x\beta t}^-(y) \right|^q
\lesssim \ve^{|\beta|-\langle\beta\rangle}
\big(\sqrt[4]{t}\big)^{\alpha-2} (\sqrt[4]{t}+|x-y|)^{\langle\beta\rangle-\alpha} \w \, .
\end{equation}

