[Prop resp-stability-G-gl of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $G$ be any compact Lie group and let $V$ be a $G$-representation. Then both adjoints in
    \[
        \Sigma^V\colon\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}_\textup{$G$-global}\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}_\textup{$G$-global}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
\Omega^V
    \]
    are homotopical, and the induced adjunction ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-gl}\rightleftarrows{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-gl}$ is an adjoint equivalence.
    \begin{proof}
        If $f$ is a $G$-global weak equivalence and $\varphi\colon H\to G$ is any homomorphism, then $\varphi^*(\Sigma^Vf)=\Sigma^{\varphi^*V}\varphi^*f$ is an $H$-equivariant weak equivalence by Proposition~(prop:rep-spheres-invertible-equiv-model of the paper). The same argument shows that $\Omega^V$ is homotopical.

        It remains to show that the unit $X\to\Omega^V\Sigma^VX$ and counit $\Sigma^V\Omega^VX\to X$ are invertible for every $X$. This follows again from Proposition~(prop:rep-spheres-invertible-equiv-model of the paper) after restricting along each group Lie group homorphism $\varphi\colon H\to G$.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem lem133 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Assume ((h of the paper)), ((f0 of the paper)) and ((f1 of the paper)) with some $\lambda>1$, let $p\ge 2$ be such that $p>n$, 
  and let $r\ge p$ be such that $r\ge\lambda$.
  Then there exist $\Gamma_8=\Gamma_8(p,r,a,h,f)>0$ as well as
  $\mu_1=\mu_1(f)>1$ and $\mu_2=\mu_2(h,f)>1$
  such that if ((init of the paper)) holds and ((uut of the paper)) is valid with some $T\in (0,T_{max}]$, then
  \begin{eqnarray}\label{133.1}
	& & \hspace*{-30mm}
	\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |u|\cdot |f(u,u_t,\nabla u,\nabla u_t)| \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2}
	+ \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |v|\cdot |f(u,u_t,\nabla u,\nabla u_t)| \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2} \nonumber\\
	&\le& \Gamma_8 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla u|^r \bigg\}^{\frac{p}{r}\cdot\mu_1}
	+ \Gamma_8 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla u|^r \bigg\}^{\frac{p}{r}\cdot\mu_2} \nonumber\\
	& & + \Gamma_8\cdot\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla v|^p \bigg\}^{\mu_1}
	+ \Gamma_8 \cdot\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla v|^p \bigg\}^{\mu_2}
	\qquad \mbox{for all } t\in (0,T).
  \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

