[Pro eq:pibar of arXiv:2411.07158, 'Markov chains on trees: almost lower and upper directed cases'] If ${\sf M}$ is the transition of an irreducible random walk on $T$, then the $h$-invariant measure of ${\sf M}$ is $\overline\pi=(\overline\pi_u,u\in T)$ defined by  $\overline{\pi}(\varnothing)=1$, and for $u\in T$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\overline{\pi}_u=\overline{\pi}(\varnothing)\prod_{j=1}^h\frac{ M_{u[j-1],u[j]}}{ M_{u[j],u[j-1]}},~~\textrm{ for } u\in T.
\end{eqnarray}
Therefore, ${\sf M}$ is positive recurrent, if and only if $\sum_{u \in T} \overline{\pi}_u<+\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

