body:
[Proposition prop:Intro:DirectionalBounds of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem (thm:Intro:ShapeHauss of the paper). Let $\Tilde{c}:S^{d-1}\to (0,+\infty)$ be defined by (equation eq:Intro:SpeedRelativeTo of the paper). There exists a positive constant $C>0$ depending on $b$, $\sigma$, $g$ and $\mathcal{M}$,  such that, for every $\epsilon\in (0,1)$, there exists $\Gamma>0$ with
        \begin{equation}
            \sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d}\probaa{x}{}{ (\mathcal{X}_t-x-t\bar{\mathbf{v}})\cap t\mathcal{H}^+_{e,(1+\epsilon)\Tilde{c}(e)} \neq \emptyset} \leq Ce^{-t\Gamma}, \ \forall\ t\geq 0, \ \mathrm{and } \  e\in S^{d-1},
        \end{equation}
        and, for every $e\in S^{d-1}$, there exists $T=T(e)>0$ with
        \begin{equation}
            \sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d}\probaa{x}{}{(\mathcal{X}_t-x-t\bar{\mathbf{v}})\subset t\mathcal{H}^-_{e, (1-\epsilon)\Tilde{c}(e)} } \leq Ce^{-t\Gamma},\ \text{for all } t>T.
        \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

