[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2512.04297, 'Mixing at the Batchelor Scale for White-In-Time Flows'] We have $\gamma_s \sim 1\wedge s$, that is, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        C^{-1} (1\wedge s) \leq \gamma_s \leq C (1\wedge s), \quad \forall\, s>0.
    \end{equation}

