[Theorem 74 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Suppose that $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times \bbr^m,\bbr^m)$ and $f \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times \bbr^m, \bbr^{m \times d})$. Then for every $\xi \in \bbr^m$ the following statements are true:
\begin{enumerate}
\item There exists a unique solution $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \beta}([0,T],W)$ to the random It\^{o} RDE \eqref{RDE-Ito-random} with $Y_0 = \xi$ on $N^c$.

\item There is a $\bbp$-nullset $N_1$ with $N \subset N_1$ such that the associated stochastic process $Y$ restricted to $N_1^c$ is also a solution to the It\^{o} SDE \eqref{SDE-Ito}.
\end{enumerate}

