[Corollary 13 (Precise isotropic kinetic tail) of arXiv:2607.07712, 'Parameter-Space Heat Flow, Gaussian Density Ratios, and Sharp Hermite Truncation Rates'] Assume
\[
g=\rho K_{u,\sigma}+h,
\qquad
\rho>0,
\qquad
0<|\sigma|<1,
\qquad
u\neq0.
\]
Suppose that
\begin{equation}
\|(I-\Pi_{\le M})h\|_{L^2(\gamma_d)}
=
o\!\left(
(M+1)^{\frac d8-\frac38}
\exp\!\left(
\frac{|u|}{|\sigma|}\sqrt{M+1}
\right)
|\sigma|^{M+1}
\right).

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
\|g-\Pi_{\le M}g\|_{L^2(\gamma_d)}
\sim
\rho
\left(
\frac{C_{d,u,\sigma}}{1-\sigma^2}
\right)^{1/2}
(M+1)^{\frac d8-\frac38}
\exp\!\left(
\frac{|u|}{|\sigma|}\sqrt{M+1}
\right)
|\sigma|^{M+1}.

\end{equation}

[Definition 8 (The Cauchy horizon) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\Cartesiantisafunctiononmumxtoriarg{0}{0},\Eikonalisafunctiononmumuxtoriarg{0}{0} : \T^2 \to \R$ be the defining scalar functions for describing the crease as a graph, namely  $\crease = \twoargmumuxtorus{0}{0} = \{ \left(\Cartesiantisafunctiononmumxtoriarg{0}{0}(x^2,x^3),\Eikonalisafunctiononmumuxtoriarg{0}{0}(x^2,x^3),x^2,x^3 \right) \, : \, (x^2,x^3) \in \T^2\}$. Then we define the  \textbf{Cauchy horizon} to be the following
subset of spacetime, where the null hypersurface portion $\ingoingcharacteristicsurfacetwoarg{0}{[\moreinterestingu_1,\moreinterestingu_2]}$ 
is defined in  \eqref{E:INTROSPACETIMEREGIONS}:
	\begin{align}
		\Cauchyhor \eqdef \left\{ (t,u,x^2,x^3)  \in  \ingoingcharacteristicsurfacetwoarg{0}{[\moreinterestingu_1,\moreinterestingu_2]} \, \Big| \, u > \Eikonalisafunctiononmumuxtoriarg{0}{0}(x^2,x^3) \, \textnormal{for all $(x^2,x^3) \in \T^2$}\right\}. 
	\end{align}

[Prop 7463 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ ( X, U ) $ be a $ ( c, q ) $-regular innovation
on a measurable set $ \mathcal V $ and let $ ( \theta_n ) $ be an \RMSprop\ algorithm
with arbitrary parameter tuple $ ( \beta, \varepsilon, (\gamma_n), \theta_0 ) $ as in the introduction.
Let $ n_0 \in {\mathbb N}_0 $ and let $ \tau $ be the stopping time given by
\bas{ 
 \tau=\inf\{n\ge n_0: \theta_n\not\in \mathcal V\}.}

One has for every $n\in{\mathbb N}_0\cap [n_0,\infty)$, $i\in\{1,\dots,d\} $, $ \lambda\in[0,\infty)$ that
\bas{
-\ln {\mathbb E}\bigl[e^{-\lambda (v_n^{(i)}+\1_{\{ n\le \tau\}^c}\infty)}|\mathcal F_{n_0}\bigr]\ge\sum_{k=n_0+1}^n \left( c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \right) \wedge q +\frac{1-\beta^{n_0}}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-n_0} \lambda  v_{n_0}^{(i)} .
}
In the case $n=n_0=0$, the last term on the right-hand side is understood as zero.

