body:
[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2605.03664, '2605.03664'] For $n=0,1,2,\dots$ and $t\geq n$,
  \begin{align}
  P(N^q(t)=n) 
  &= \lambda^n \sum_{m=0}^\infty \binom{n+m}{n} (-\lambda)^m 
  \cdot\Big[ \hat{h}_{q(n+m)}(t-n+1) + \lambda \hat{h}_{q(n+m+1)-1}(t-n+1) \Big].
\end{align}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:d2a7f48b5e15383f420bb9e97261efae8d36614385688c9a024c8368e675cac9","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/d2/d2a7f48b5e15383f420bb9e97261efae8d36614385688c9a024c8368e675cac9.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:e97f6a2e479fc982d98ea30da46acade3b1f8a8696c0060e11d5d777756a1fb5","bundle_entry_key":"2605-03664-theorem-1-theorem-1","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_026","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_026.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-03664-theorem-1-theorem-1","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The event that the counting process $N^q(t)$ is in state $n$ means that exactly $n$ arrivals occur up to time $t$, which can be expressed using the arrival times as follows:
\begin{align}
  P(N(t) = n) = P(S_n \le t) - P(S_{n+1} \le t).
\end{align}
Thus, letting $H^q_n(z) := \sum_{t=0}^\infty P(N(t)=n) z^t$, we have
\begin{align}
  H^q_n(z) &= \sum_{t=0}^\infty P(S_n \le t) z^t - \sum_{t=0}^\infty P(S_{n+1} \le t) z^t \nonumber \\
  &=\frac{E[z^{S_n}]}{1-z} - \frac{E[z^{S_{n+1}}]}{1-z}
  \\
  &= \frac{G^q(z)^n}{1-z} - \frac{G^q(z)^{n+1}}{1-z} \nonumber \\
  &= \frac{G^q(z)^n (1 - G^q(z))}{1-z} 
  \\
