[Corollary cor:optimal of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For each $\alpha>0$, there exists a constant $c_\alpha$ such that for any label-invariant estimator $\widehat{\sigma}$, and any $n\ge 2$,
    \begin{equation*}
        R_{\alpha}(\widehat{\sigma}) \ge 
        \begin{dcases}
            c_\alpha n^{2-\alpha}, &\text{if }\alpha\in(0,2),\\
            c_\alpha\log n,&\text{if }\alpha=2, \\
            c_\alpha,&\text{if }\alpha>2.
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

