[Theorem 18 (\citet{GLSS}) of arXiv:2605.24445, 'Matrix concentration inequalities for time-inhomogeneous Markov chains'] Let \(H_{1},\dots,H_n\in\Hm\). Then, there exists a probability measure $\nu$ on  $[-\pi/2,\pi/2]$ such that
\begin{equation}
\tr\exp\Big(\frac{\pi}{4} \, \sum_{t=1}^n H_t\Big)
\;\le\;
 m^{1-\pi/4}\,
 \int_{-\pi/2}^{\pi/2}
\tr\Bigg(\prod_{t=1}^n e^{\frac{1}{2}e^{i\phi}H_t} \,
\prod_{t=n}^1 e^{\frac{1}{2}e^{-i\phi}H_t}\Bigg)\,\nu(\phi).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

