		Let $u_R^{(m)}$ be the solution of (equation truncated_eq of the paper) constructed in Proposition (localwellres of the paper) with initial data $u_0^m$ and noise kernel $k_m$. By Young's inequality, it is clear that for any $s\geq 0$ we have ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:b434a147cd47983a55765907292d91af233132060002e9bd537550fd40d70b4d","revision_digest":"sha256:64a9528b7f9d4749fe41fd8ca1a56045aa0f098da31b55aeb9de8744dc1ce6bb","source_id":"arxiv:2606.31155","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

