{"artifact_digest":"sha256:324e3f65f9bdd6fd77c006d3ab4031f55dd787d07394bd4078f3b78efd07ba0d","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/32/324e3f65f9bdd6fd77c006d3ab4031f55dd787d07394bd4078f3b78efd07ba0d.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:97e28ce81b41c16a34bdf446577a283657aa47381dbfd51169d8eb6e10754ee0","bundle_entry_key":"2608-25706-lemma-29-uniformly-bounded-predictive-v","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_108","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_108.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-25706-lemma-29-uniformly-bounded-predictive-v","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The exact posterior covariance kernel is
    \begin{align*}
    \sK_t(x,x')= \sK_0(x,x')
    -\sK_0(x, X_{1:t})(\sigma_\xi^2 I + \sK_0(X_{1:t},X_{1:t}))^{-1} \sK_0( X_{1:t},x').
    \end{align*}
Consequently,
    \begin{align*}
    0\le v_{\Pi_t}(x)=\sK_t(x,x)\le \sK_0(x,x).
    \end{align*}
For the variational posterior, \eqref{eq:gp-q-covariance} gives
    \begin{align*}
    v_{Q_t^{(J)}}(x)
    =\sK_t^{(J)}(x,x)
    =\sK_0(x,x)-\psi_{1:J}(x)^\top\del{\Lambda_J-V_{t,J}}\psi_{1:J}(x)
    \end{align*}
Since
    \begin{align*}
    V_{t,J}^{-1}
    =  \Lambda_J^{-1} + \sigma_\xi^{-2}\Psi_{t,J}^\top\Psi_{t,J}
    \succeq  \Lambda_J^{-1},
