[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.24684, 'Waning Immunity Fails to Restore a Positive Epidemic Threshold on Power--Law Networks'] Let $G_\star$ denote the star graph on vertex set $\{v,u_1,\dots, u_k\}$ with center $v$. 
Define the random set $U_v$ by
\begin{align*}
U_v
:=\Big\{ u\in \{u_1,\dots, u_k\}:
N^{\mathrm{sus}}_{u}\big((0,\tfrac12 k^{-1/3})\big)\ge 1,\ 
N^{\mathrm{inf}}_{v\to u}\big([\tfrac12 k^{-1/3},\,k^{-1/3}]\big)\ge 1, 
N^{\mathrm{rec}}_{u}\big([0,(\log k)/4)\big)=0
\Big\},
\end{align*}
and define the event
\begin{equation}
A_2^{(v)}:=\{|U_v|\ge k^{1/24}\},
\end{equation}
where $N^{\mathrm{sus}}_{u}$, $N^{\mathrm{inf}}_{v\to u}$, and $N^{\mathrm{rec}}_{u}$ are the Poisson clocks in the modified Harris construction.
Then, $U_v, A_2^{(v)}$ are $\mathcal{G}(v, \{u_1,\dots, u_k\})$ measurable, with $\mathcal{G}(v, \{u_1,\dots, u_k\})$ defined in Definition~\ref{def:local_graphical_data}, and for all sufficiently large $k$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\!\left( A_{2}^{(v)}\right)
\ \ge\ 1-\exp\!\big(-k^{1/24}\big).
\end{equation}

[Corollary Phi-strong-align of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] For every $n\geq 0$, the unique interior fixed
point $\phi _{n+1}\in (0,1)$ of $\Phi _{n+1}$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\min \{\,L_{n+1}(c_{n}),\,c_{n+1}\,\}\ \leq \ \phi _{n+1}\ \leq \ \max
\{\,L_{n+1}(c_{n}),\,c_{n+1}\,\}.  
\end{equation}

[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given~$n\ge1$, let~$\ell^{(n)}_{\tau_\varrho}$ be the local time on~$\T_n$ for the walk started from~$\zero\in\BbbL_n$ and stopped upon first hit of~$\varrho$. Then for all~$1\le k\le n$, 
\begin{equation}

\bigl\{\ell^{(n)}_{\tau_\varrho}(x)\colon x\in\T_k\bigr\}\laweq \bigl\{\ell^{(k)}_{\tau_\varrho}(x)\colon x\in\T_k\bigr\}.
\end{equation}
In particular, the laws of $\{\ell^{(n)}_{\tau_\varrho}\colon n\ge1\}$ are Kolmogorov-consistent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:SAW-Pip of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 5$ and $a \in [0,2d-4]$.
For any choice of $p \in [1,\infty]$ satisfying
\begin{equation} 
\frac 1 p < 1 + \frac{ \frac 3 2 d - 4 - a } d ,
\end{equation}
there is a constant $K_{a,p} < \infty$ such that
\begin{equation}

\bignorm{ \abs x^a  \Pi_z ^{(\mu)}(x)  }_p  \le  K_{a,p}
\end{equation}
uniformly in $z \in [z_c - \delta, z_c)$ and in $\mu \in \overline \Omega_z$.
For $a = 2d-4$, (equation eq:Pi_moments-pnorm of the paper) also holds with $p = 2$.

