body:
[Dfn indices of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] Let $H=(V,E)$ be a graph with node set $V$ and edge set $E$.\\
    The Zagreb index is defined as
    \begin{align}
        Z_H:=\sum_{v \in V} (d(v))^2.
    \end{align}
For $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$, the  $\alpha$-Randić index of $H$ is given by
    \begin{align}
        R_H^{[\alpha]}:=\sum_{\{u,v\} \in E} (d(u)d(v))^\alpha.
    \end{align}
If $H$ is connected, the Wiener index is defined as  
    \begin{align}
        W_H:=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{u,v\in V} \dist(u,v).
    \end{align}
If $H$ is connected and rooted, the level index is defined as 
    \begin{align}
        L_{H}:=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{u,v \in V} \vert D(u)-D(v)\vert.
    \end{align}
For a random graph $H$ of a class of rooted, connected graphs $\mathcal{H}$, the Gini index is given by
\begin{align}
G_H:=\frac{L_{H}}{\,{\mathbb{E}}[V]^2\,{\mathbb{E}}[D_\mathcal{H}^\star]},
\end{align}
where $D_\mathcal{H}^\star$ is the depth of a randomly chosen node in a random tree of class $\mathcal{H}$ (see [ma17] for more information).

