[Lemma lem:extra:4-ST of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Suppose that \((T,R_{+},R_{-},\gamma)\) is a 4-ST. Then up to orbit equivalence, there is only one semiflow \(\varphi\) satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(\varphi\) is tight.
\item \(\varphi\) contains exactly one bi-infinite flowline \(\lambda\) and \(\lambda\) is a pseudo-hyperbolic closed orbit.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:one-step-reduction of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Fix a deterministic time \(t\ge0\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and suppose that
for some fixed \(K>K_2^{\mathrm{ER}}(b)\),
\begin{align}
\Delta_t\ge K\frac{N}{\sqrt{\log N}}.

\end{align}
Then, for any fixed \(r\) satisfying
\begin{align}
q_K<r<r_*,

\end{align}
we have, for all sufficiently large \(N\),
\begin{align}
\P\left(
|\gR_{t+1}|\le rN
\,\middle|\,
\rvy_t
\right)
\ge
1-2\exp\left(-\left(\log N\right)^2\right).

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma l:Theta-bound of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] For any $B\in {\mathrm{SL}}(2,{\mathbb R})$ and any nonzero vector $v\in {\mathbb R}^2$, one has
\begin{equation}
\Theta(B, v)\le -\log \sin{\rm dist}([v],\mathbf{r}(B)).
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:overlap of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] The following holds on a single event of full probability. Let $(p_n;q_n) = (x_n,s_n;y_n,u_n) \in \mathbb{R}_{{\scaleobj{0.7}{\uparrow}}}^4 \to (p;q) = (x,s;y,u) \in \mathbb{R}_{{\scaleobj{0.7}{\uparrow}}}^4$, and let $g_n$ be any sequence of geodesics from $p_n$ to $q_n$. Suppose that either
\begin{enumerate} [label=\rm(\roman{*}), ref=\rm(\roman{*})]  \itemsep=3pt
    \item  For all $n$, $(x_n,s_n;y_n,u_n) \in \mathbb{R}_{{\scaleobj{0.7}{\uparrow}}}^4 \cap \mathbb{Q}^4$, or
    \item  There is a unique geodesic $g$ from $p$ to $q$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, the \textbf{overlap}
    \[
    O(g_n,g) := \{t \in [s_n,u_n]\cap [s,u]: g_n(t) = g(t)\}    
    \]
    is an interval for all $n$ whose endpoints converge to $s$ and $u$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma CC03+ of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] For any  $1\geqslant {\beta_x}, {\beta_v}\geqslant0$ so that $\frac{\beta_x}{1+\alpha},\beta_v<\alpha-1$ and $m,n\in{\mathbb N}$ so that $m+n\leqslant1$, 
       there exist constants $C=C(d,{\beta_x},{\beta_v},m,n)$ such that for any $t\in(0,1]$,
\begin{align}

&\big\||x|^{\frac{\beta_x}{1+\alpha}}|v|^{\beta_v}|\nabla_x^m\nabla_v^n\partial_t(\Gamma_t\rho_t)(x,v)|\big\|_{1}\leqslant C  t^{\frac{\beta_x-(\alpha+1)m+(\beta_v-n)-\alpha}{\alpha}

}.
\end{align}

