[Lem ideal of arXiv:2411.09640, 'Random Lipschitz functions on graphs with weak expansion'] There is a constant $C$ for which the following holds. For any $\gamma>C$, if $k>\gamma M^2\log(Mn)$, then for $\mathbf{f}$ chosen uniformly at random from $\mbox{\rm{Lip}}_{v_0}(C_{n,k}; M)$, for any $v \in V$,
\begin{equation}\label{nonideal}
\mathbb{P}(|\bar\mathbf{f}_{N_v^+}| \ne M+1) = O((\gamma n)^{-1}).
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $\log M=o_n(\log n)$, then
\begin{equation}\label{nonideal'}
\mathbb{P}(|\bar\mathbf{f}_{N_v^+}| \ne M+1) = o_n(n^{-1}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

