[Proposition prop:Legendre of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] The following holds for almost-every $\omega$. Let $b$ be an eternal solution, and let $\varphi$ be the unique element of $\Phi_\omega$ such that $b = W\star \varphi$, as in Proposition (prop:uniq of the paper). Then, 
     \begin{equation}
        \varphi(\xi)=\inf_{(x,t)\in\mathbb{R}^2}\{b(x,t)-W^\xi(0,0;x,t)\}, \qquad \forall \xi\in \mathfrak{X}.
     \end{equation}

