[Lem 21 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] For $y\in \R$ and $f\in C_c^\infty(\R)$, we have
\begin{align}
   \int_\R h(x-y)|\widehat{\mathscr{L}}f(x)|\,dx<\infty.
\end{align}
Consequently, 
\begin{align}
\langle \mathscr{L} h(\cdot-y),f\rangle =\int_\R h(x-y)\widehat{\mathscr{L}}f(x)dx
\end{align}
is well-defined.

