body:
[Corollary 31 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $a_n(G)$ be the number of $\Sn_n$-spherical irreducible representations of $W_n(G)$, and let $f_n(G)$ be the number of these representations self-dual.  Then every minimal gap-determining family for $W_n(G)$ has cardinality $(a_n(G)+f_n(G))/2$.  Moreover,
\begin{align}
a_n(G)
&=[t^n]
\prod_{\gamma\in\Gamma}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^j},
\\
f_n(G)
&=[t^n]
\prod_{\substack{\gamma\in\Gamma\\\gamma\cong\gamma^*}}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^j}
\prod_{\{\gamma,\gamma^*\}:\,\gamma\not\cong\gamma^*}
\prod_{j=1}^{d_\gamma}\frac{1}{1-t^{2j}}.

\end{align}
In the second product of \eqref{eq:general-fixed-count}, each unordered dual pair is taken once. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:abstract-positive-response-gram of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For a faithfully potential-realizable response, let
$\Lambda_{n_1}^\mu,\ldots,\Lambda_{n_M}^\mu$ be distinct simple positive
eigenvalues whose centered response measures
$\eta_{n_i}^\mu$ are linearly independent in
$\mathcal M_{\rm resp}(\mu)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \left(
 \inner{U_\mu\eta_{n_i}^\mu}
        {U_\mu\eta_{n_j}^\mu}_{H}
 \right)_{i,j=1}^M

\end{equation}
defines a positive-definite matrix.

