[Prop opti_problem_231 of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] The action $A_{\beta}$ has a unique minimizer $\varphi_\beta$ in $\mathcal{E}$. 
    Moreover, for $\beta \leq 0$, we have $\varphi_{\beta}(t)=0$ for all $t \in [0,1]$. 
    For $\beta>0$, it is given by the formula
	\begin{equation}
		\varphi_\beta(t)= \frac{1}{\beta} \log\left( \frac{ 1 + \textup{e}^{\beta} }{ 1 + \textup{e}^{\beta(1-2t)}} \right) - t.
	\end{equation}

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2605.26439, '2605.26439'] Let $T>0$. Assume that $B\in\mathcal L(U;\mathcal H_{-\eta})$ for some $\eta\in[0,1)$ and that there exists $\beta\in(0,1/2)$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \int_0^T t^{-2\beta}\|S_{-\eta}(t)B\|_{\mathcal L_2(U;\mathcal H)}^2dt<\infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then the stochastic convolution
    \begin{equation*}
        W_A(t):=\int_0^tS_{-\eta}(t-s)BdW_s,\quad t\in[0,T],
    \end{equation*}
    is well defined and admits an $\mathcal H$-valued continuous modification. Moreover,
    \begin{equation*}
        W_A\in L^2(\Omega;C([0,T];\mathcal H)).
    \end{equation*}

