[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] For any $\psi \in H^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $q > 1$ such that $d(q-1) < 2q$, there exists some $\theta \in (0, 1)$ such that
    \begin{equation}  

    \| \psi^2 \ast p_{\epsilon} - \psi^2 \|_q \le C \epsilon^{\theta/2} \| \nabla \psi \|_2^{2 - \theta} \| \psi \|_2^{\theta} \le C \epsilon^{\theta/2} ( \| \nabla \psi \|_2^2 + \| \psi \|_2^2).
    \end{equation}
    Similarly, for $\psi^1 , \dots , \psi^p \in H^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ such that $d(p-1) < 2p$,
    \begin{equation}

        \bigg\| \Big(\prod_{j=1}^p \psi^j\Big)^2 - \Big(\prod_{j=1}^p (\psi^j)^2 \ast p_{\epsilon} \Big) \bigg\|_1 \le C \epsilon^{\theta/2} \Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^p ( \| \nabla \psi^j \|_2^2 + \| \psi^j \|_2^2 ) \Bigr)^p.
    \end{equation}

