[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $E$ be another Banach space. Then for all
\begin{align*}
(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W) \quad \text{and} \quad (Z,Z') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],E)
\end{align*}
we have the relation
\begin{align}
((Y,Z),(Y,Z)') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W \times E),
\end{align}
where the Gubinelli derivative is given by $(Y,Z)' = (Y',Z')$, and we have the estimates
\begin{align}
\| (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' \|_{X,2\alpha} &\leq \| Y,Y' \|_{X,2\alpha} + \| Z,Z' \|_{X,2\alpha},
\\  | (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' |_{X,2\alpha} &\leq | Y,Y' |_{X,2\alpha} + | Z,Z' |_{X,2\alpha},
\\  \interleave (Y,Z), (Y,Z)' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} &\leq \interleave Y,Y' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} + \interleave Z,Z' \interleave_{X,2\alpha}.
\end{align}

