[Lemma Closed blocks of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:closed_blocks}
    Let $b \in \mathbf{N}$ and let $A_0,\ldots,A_{b-1}$ be a $1$-disconnected sequence of $1$-connected sets.

    Then there exists $\ell \leq b$ and $(B_0,\ldots,B_{\ell-1}) \in \mathcal{A}(\ell)$ such that $\cup_{i \leq b} A_i \subset \cup_{j \leq \ell} B_j$ and $\cup_{j \leq \ell} \partial B_j \subset \cup_{i \leq b} \partial A_i$.

