body:
[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] For all $n,k\geq1$, $T>0$, $x\in E$ and $y\in\mathbb R^d$ we set
\begin{align*}
\phi_T^{n,k}(y,x)=\mathbf E_{x}\big[\varphi(\mathbf Z_T^{n,y})\,\mathbf 1_{\{T\leq\tau_k^n\}}\big].
\end{align*}
Let $L>0$, then for all $n,k\geq1$, $T>0$ there exist $M_T^k>0$ such that for all $z,y\in\mathbb R^d$ and $x\in E$
\begin{align*}
\lvert\phi_T^{n,k}(y,x)-\phi_T^{n,k}(z,x)\rvert&\leq2\,\|\varphi\|_\infty\,\mathbf P_x(T\leq\tau_k^n,L_T^n>L)+\|\nabla\varphi\|_\infty\,\lvert y-z\rvert\,e^{TL}
\end{align*}
where for all $t>0$ and $n\geq1$
\begin{align*}
L_t^n:=\sup_{s\in[0,t]}L_{\mathbf I_s^n}.
\end{align*}

