[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.22595, 'Sparse Additive Off-Policy Evaluation for Reinforcement Learning with Potentially Limited '] There exist positive constants $c_3$ and $c_4$ and a good event
$\mathcal{G}_2$ satisfying
\[
P(\mathcal{G}_2)
\geq
1-\exp\left\{-c_4\log(nT\vee d)\right\}
\]
such that, on $\mathcal{G}_2$,
\[
\left\|
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Sigma}}
-
\boldsymbol{\Sigma}
\right\|_{\max}
\leq
c_3L\log(nT\vee d)
\sqrt{
\frac{\log(nT\vee d)}{nT}
}.
