body:
[Proposition prop:so-nn of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d>2$,
$\eta >0$,
$L \ge L_2$ (with $L_2$ sufficiently large),
and $\mu\in [\frac{1}{2},1)$.
Then
\begin{align}
m_S(\mu)^2 \sim \frac{2d}{\sigma_L^2} (1-\mu)
	\qquad \text{as $\mu\to 1$,}
\end{align}
and there are constants $K_S > 0$, $a_S \in (0,1)$ (independent of $L$)
and $\delta_2 = \delta_2(L) > 0$, such that
\begin{equation}
S_\mu(x) \le \delta_{0,x} +
	\frac {K_S}{ L^{1-\eta} \nnnorm x^{d-2} } e^{- a_S m_S(\mu) \norm x_\infty }
	\qquad (x\in \mathbb Z^d)
\end{equation}
uniformly in $\mu \in [1 - \delta_2, 1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

