[Lemma lem:tree of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There is a tree $T = ([d], E)$ such that for every edge $e = (i,j) \in E$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \Ps{\sigma \sim \mu}{i \text{ and } j \text{ are in the same cycle in the cycle decomposition of } \sigma} \geqslant \frac{1}{d} \Phi_{\ast}.
    \end{equation*}

