[Prop key proposition for soft error term of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $O_n$ be the event defined in (equation definition of O_n of the paper) and $S_n, \overset{\sim}{S}_n$ be the random walks defined in (equation def of S_n and S_n hat of the paper). Then, for some absolute constant $C$, conditional on $X_0,X_3, \cdots, X_n$, 
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{E}_2\left[\frac{1}{|(X_0-X_2)S_n|^2} \mathbbm{1}_{O_n} 
     \right] \leq C \min \left \{ 1, \frac{\log(1+2|\overset{\sim}{S}_n|)}{|\overset{\sim}{S}_n|^2}  \right \}\mathbbm{1}_{X_0 \in \mathbb{A}_n}.
    \end{align}

