[Coro local_time_approx of arXiv:2411.05441, 'Sticky diffusions on star graphs : characterization and It\^o formula'] Let $f \colon \mathbb{R}_+ \to \mathbb{R}$ be bounded and continuous and let $X(t) = (i(t),x(t))$ be a sticky process on $\Gamma$ with generator (equation generator of the paper)-(equation eq:domain of the paper) and stickiness parameter $\eta$, started at $\mathsf{v}$. Define, for $\delta > 0$, the collections of stopping times $(\tau_n^\delta)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $(\theta_n^\delta)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ by $\tau_0^\delta = \theta_0^\delta = 0$ and
		\begin{equation}
		\begin{split}
			\theta_n^\delta = \inf \left \{ t \geq \tau_{n-1}^\delta : x(t) = \delta \right \},  \\
			\tau_n^\delta = \inf \left \{ t \geq \theta_{n}^\delta : x(t) = 0 \right \},
		\end{split}
		\end{equation}
		for $n \geq 1$. Then, for every $t \geq 0$,
		\[
		 \lim_{\delta \to 0} \delta \sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}} f(\theta_{n+1}^\delta) \mathbf{1}_{\{\theta_{n+1}^\delta \leq t \}} = \int_0^t f(s) d \ell_X(s) \quad \textnormal{in probability}.
		\]
		In particular
		\[
		 \lim_{\delta \to 0} \delta \sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \mathbf{1}_{\{\theta_{n+1}^\delta \leq t \}} = \ell_X(t) \quad \textnormal{in probability.}
		\]

