[Definition 6 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] For $f \in L^{1}_{loc}(\R^{d})$, the Hardy--Littlewood maximal function $\mathcal{M}(f)(x)$ is defined by
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal{M}(f)(x)=\sup_{r>0}\frac{1}{|B(x,r)|}\int_{B(x,r)}|f(y)|dy.
\end{equation*}

