body:
[Proposition prop:stiff-pointwise of arXiv:2603.14906, 'Four Levels of Thermodynamic Convergence of Singularly Perturbed Markov Semigroups'] Suppose (ass:stiff-geom of the paper) holds and that $\nabla V$ is locally Lipschitz with at most linear growth, so that (equation eq:stiff-nl-SDE of the paper) is non-explosive.
Let $G:=I+H^\top H$ and $\bar V(u):=V(\iota(u))=V(Hu+b,u)$.
Let $(\bar P_t)_{t\ge0}$ denote the Markov semigroup on $\bar E$ with generator
\begin{equation}
  \bar{\mathcal L}g(u)=\mathrm{tr}\!\big(G^{-1}\nabla^2 g(u)\big)-\big\langle G^{-1}\nabla\bar V(u),\,\nabla g(u)\big\rangle,
  \qquad g\in C_c^\infty(\bar E),
\end{equation}
equivalently, the semigroup of the diffusion
\begin{equation}
  dU_t=-G^{-1}\nabla \bar V(U_t)\,dt+\sqrt{2}\,G^{-1/2}\,dB_t,\qquad U_0=u\in\bar E.
\end{equation}
Then for every $t>0$, every $f\in C_b(E)$ and every $z\in E$,
\begin{equation}
  P_t^\varepsilon f(z)\longrightarrow \bar P_t(\mathcal P f)\big(\Phi(z)\big)
  \qquad\text{as }\varepsilon\downarrow0.
\end{equation}

