[Definition of arXiv:2606.13264, 'Interference Queueing Networks: A Replica Mean-Field Approach in the Symmetric Setting'] We say that $Q$ is associated if for any $f$ and $g$ increasing real function for the partial order on $\mathbb{N}^N$, and $t \in \mathbb{R}^+ $
    \begin{align}
        &\mathbb{P}^{Q(t)}(fg)\geq \mathbb{P}^{Q(t)}(f)\mathbb{P}^{Q(t)}(g) \Leftrightarrow \mathbb{E}[f(Q(t))g(Q(t))]\geq\mathbb{E}[f(Q(t))]\mathbb{E}[g(Q(t))]
    \end{align}

[Lemma measure_tau2_u_v of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Let $(\tau,\tau';v,v') \in \mathfrak{P}^{i,j,\ell}$. 
We have
\begin{equation}
	\mu^{i,j,\ell}_{\mathbf{Y},\mathbf{Y}'}(\tau,\tau';v,v') = 
	\frac{1}{\prod_{x\in \mathcal{F}_\ell(\tau,\tau';v,v')} n_x!}
	e^{-f_\ell(\tau,\tau';v,v')},
\end{equation}
	where for all $x \in V(\tau)\cup V(\tau')$, $n_x$ is the number of children of the vertex $x$ in the corresponding tree.

