body:
[Theorem thm:moment-evolution of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For $t \leq t_*$ and edge indices $i$ with $|\lambda_i - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon/2}$:
\begin{align}
\left|\mathbb{E}[(X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t))^2] - 1\right| &\leq C_2 N^{-1/6+\varepsilon}\\
\left|\mathbb{E}[(X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t))^4] - 3\right| &\leq C_3 N^{-1/6+\varepsilon}
\end{align}
where $C_2 = 5d^2\varepsilon^{-8}$ and $C_3 = 12d^3\varepsilon^{-10}$.

