body:
[Theorem mainth of arXiv:2609.02541, 'A note on the norm of the embedding of $\text{PW}^2$ into $\text{PW}^q$'] For any $q>2$
    \begin{align*}
    M_q = \sup_{\substack{f\in PW^2\\ \|f\|_2=1}}\|f\|_q^q \leq \Lambda_q := \int_0^{\infty} (\lambda'(x))^{q/2}dx,
    \end{align*}
where $\lambda(s)$ denotes the best $L^2$ concentration in $PW^2$ on $[-s/2,s/2]$, i.e.,
$$\lambda(s):=\sup_{\substack{f\in PW^2\\ \lVert f\rVert_2=1}}
 \int_{-s/2}^{s/2}|f(x)|^2 dx.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

