Thus, the claim follows from the self-adjointness of $A_{-1/2}$ as well as the well-known identity $\mathscr{X}_{1/2}^{A}(B)=\mathbb{H}^1_0(B)$ (see [NVW13] and","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:b7eb0ea8b6da164400b87f9fcb9c9254c235b00b8e31ee7d71d7d8d596a443b9","revision_digest":"sha256:72209881de27780adaebf93e5297798ad1cf78ff3a10d52bc9e1addeb3db9643","source_id":"arxiv:2607.15140","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

