body:
[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2608.25925 (problem environment labelled prob:recursive-alpha).] Construct a canonical family of monotone domain operators $\Theta_\alpha$ for recursive ordinals $\alpha$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item the fixed point of $\Theta_\alpha$ contains exactly an intended initial segment of the transfinite jump hierarchy;
\item its closure rank is invariant under the chosen representation of $\alpha$, up to an explicitly characterized ordinal transformation;
\item failures of Scott continuity occur precisely at effective limit-uniformization nodes.
\end{enumerate} (Verbatim from the paper's TeX; symbols are the source paper's. Stated as open/conjectural; no resolution of it was found in the paper's own text by the rules of problem_index.py - a paper may still prove special cases of a conjecture it states.)

[Theorem thm:abstract-simple-splitting of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Under (equation eq:countable-direction-space of the paper) and
(equation eq:direction-annihilator of the paper), for every multiple positive
eigenvalue $\Lambda$ of $A_\mu$ there exists $q\in\mathcal Q$ such that
\begin{equation}
 B_q^\Lambda(\mu)
 =-\kappa\LambdaP_\Lambda^\mu
 \operatorname{Mult}_q|_{E_\mu(\Lambda)}

\end{equation}
has simple spectrum.  Writing $r=\dim E_\mu(\Lambda)$, let
$\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_r$ be the real-analytic eigenvalue branches issuing
from $\Lambda$ along $d\mu_\tau=e^{\kappa\tau q}\,d\mu$, so that
$\lambda_j(0)=\Lambda$ for $1\le j\le r$.  Then
\begin{equation*}
 \lambda_i'(0)\ne\lambda_j'(0),
 \qquad 1\le i<j\le r.
\end{equation*}

[Lemma lem:path_prob of arXiv:2605.06511, 'Logarithmic Mixing of Random Walks on Dynamical Random Cluster Models'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ be sufficiently large and $G = (V, E)$ a $d$-regular graph on $n$ vertices. For all $\mu > 0$, $t \geq 0$, $x > 0$, $e = \{u, u'\} \in E$ such that $B_R(u)$ has at most one cycle, and $(\eta, v) \in \{0, 1\}^E \times V$, then
		\begin{align*}
			& \mathbb{P}\left[\xi_{u, e}^{\mathrm{path}}\left(t, t + x\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right] \\
			\geq&\ \left(1 - 2K \left(p + (1-p)e^{-\mu x}\right)^{{R}/{2}}\right) \mathbb{P}\left[S_{t+x} \left(R, K\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right].
		\end{align*}

