[Definition 3 of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] After choosing the normal so that $H\geq n\kappa$, a hypersurface satisfies the
\emph{quantitative $\tau$-bi-Ricci pinching condition} with constant
$\alpha_0>0$ if
\begin{equation}
 P_{ij}^{(\tau)}
 \geq\alpha_0 H|\lambda_p-\lambda_q|
 \qquad(i\ne j,\ p,q\text{ arbitrary}).
\end{equation}

[Lem 8 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:main} it holds that
    \begin{equation}
        \sup\limits_{t\geq 0} 
        \left(
        \mathbb{E}\left[
        \Vert X_t\Vert_2 ^p
        \right]
        \right)^{1/p}
        \leq \left(
        \sqrt{3}
        \left(
            \mathbb{E}\left[
        \Vert X_0\Vert_2^p
        \right]
        \right)^{1/p}
        +6 
        \sqrt{\frac{6C_{\mathrm{BDG}}}{\varkappa}}
        + 
        \sqrt{\frac{3d}{\varkappa}}
        \right)
        \sqrt{p}, 
        \quad p\geq 2,
    \end{equation}
    where \(C_{\mathrm{BDG}}\) is the constant from the Burkholder-Davis-Gundy inequality depending only on \(p\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 9 of arXiv:2604.26316, 'Smallest distances between zeros of Gaussian analytic functions'] As $n\to\infty$, one has the convergence,  $$
		\abs{\tilde{\mathcal I}_n}
		\stackrel{\text { }}- \abs{\mathcal I_n}\to0 \,\, \mbox{ in probability. }$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

