Thus the path $t\mapsto X_t^{(m)}(\omega)$ is piecewise constant on the above dyadic intervals. In particular, it is right-continuous on each interval and has finite left limits at each grid point. Since also $X_T^{(m)}(\omega)=X_T(\omega)$, the path is c\`adl\`ag on $[0,T]$. \vspace{.2cm}

