body:
[Theorem UniformFCLT of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] (Asymptotic equicontinuity)\\

For $\nu > 2, \kappa \in (0, 1/2 - 1/\nu), C \geq 0$ and finite functions $R,J: (0,\infty) \to [0,\infty)$ let
\begin{equation*}
\gamma(m, \delta) = C m \left(R(\delta) + J(\delta) m^{-\kappa} \right)^2, ~ m \in \mathbb N, \delta > 0.
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, let $(\mathcal F, \rho)$ be totally bounded and suppose that for all $\delta > 0$ and $n \in \mathbb N$, it holds
\begin{equation}
\EOuter{ \norm{ S_{n,i,j} }_{\mathcal F_\delta}^\nu } \leq \gamma^{\frac{\nu}{2}}(j-i+1,\delta), ~ \forall ~ 1 \leq i \leq j \leq n,
\end{equation}
and that there exists $f_0 \in \mathcal F$ with
\begin{equation}
\norm{S_{n,i,j}(f_0)}_{L_\nu} \leq C \sqrt{j-i+1}, ~ \forall ~ 1 \leq i \leq j \leq n.
\end{equation}  
If $\lim_{\delta \downarrow 0} R(\delta) = 0$, then (equation DEF:AEC of the paper) holds for $\tau$ from (equation UFCLT-tau of the paper) and fidi-convergence of $\mathbb Z_n$ implies weak convergence in $\ell^{\infty}([0,1] \times \mathcal F)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

