[Theorem thm:weak-type-LDP of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] Let assumptions (ass:finite-plan-exists of the paper) and (ass:bernton44mod of the paper) hold.
    If $c_\eta \to c$ uniformly over $\mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Y}$ as ${\eta \downarrow 0}$, then we get that the sequence $\{ \pi_\eta \}_{\eta > 0}$ satisfies a ``weak-type'' LDP with rate function $I: \calX \times \calY \to [0, \infty]$ given by 
    \begin{equation}
        I(x, y) \coloneq \sup_{k \geq 2} \sup_{(x_i, y_i)_{2=1}^k \subseteq \Gamma} \sup_{\sigma \in \Sigma(k)} \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_i) - \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_{\sigma(i)}),
    \end{equation}
    This means that we have:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item 
        For any open set $G \subseteq \calX_0 \times \calY_0$,
        \begin{equation*}
            -\inf_{(x,y) \in G} I(x,y) \leq \liminf_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta(G).
        \end{equation*}
        \item For any compact set $K \subseteq \calX \times \calY$,
        \begin{equation*}
            \limsup_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta(K) \leq -\inf_{(x,y) \in K} I(x,y).
        \end{equation*}
    \end{enumerate}
    Further, for any Kantorovich potential $\psi$, $I = c - (-\psi \oplus \psi^c)$ on $\calX_0 \times \calY_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm_main of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] Assume (equation converging_ratios of the paper), (equation delta_decay of the paper), (equation balanced of the paper). 
Then for either ${\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}\in\{\mathsf{Ising},\mathsf{spherical}\}$ we have
\eeq{
\liminf_{N \to \infty} F_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}(\vc\Delta,\vc\lambda_N)\geqslant \lim_{N\to\infty} F_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}^\mathsf{single}(\boldsymbol{\beta}),
}
where the coordinates of $\boldsymbol{\beta} = (\beta_p)_{p\geqslant1}$ are given by
\eeq{ 
\beta_p^2 \coloneqq \sum_{s_1,\dots,s_p\in\mathscr{S}}
\Delta^2_{s_1,\dots,s_p}\lambda_{s_1}\cdots\lambda_{s_p}.
}
Furthermore,
\eeq{ 
\liminf_{N\to\infty} \GSE_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}(\vc\Delta,\vc\lambda_N)\geqslant \lim_{N\to\infty} \GSE_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}^{\mathsf{single}} (\boldsymbol{\beta}).
} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

