(T,1,\bm L,\bm k,\bm{\mathcal P},\bm C,\bm m)$ such that $f_{R,\lambda}(\bm X)=\mathcal R(\bm X)-\lambda$ for every $\bm X\in\mathbb R^T$. Consequently, $h_{R,\lambda}\in
