[Theorem thKM of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $\eta$ be an offspring distribution such that $\eta(0) >0$ and $\eta(1) >0$ and denote by $F$ its generating function. Let $(S_n)_{n\geq0}$ be a random walk started from $S_0=0$ with step distribution $\eta$. Assume $k_n=o(n)$ and $k_n\rightarrow \infty$. Then
    \begin{equation}
    \sup_{k\geq -k_n} \left| \sqrt{k_n} \frac{b_n^{k_n+k}}{F(b_n)^{n-k_n}}\mathbb{P}\left(S_{n-k_n} = k_n+k\right) - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{k^2}{2k_n}}\right| \xrightarrow[n \rightarrow \infty]{} 0,
\end{equation}
where $b_n$ is defined by
 \[b_n\frac{F'(b_n)}{F(b_n)}=\frac{k_n}{n-k_n}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

