[Definition def:supermartingale of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequential gamble space.
  A sequence $\{X_t:\mathcal{Y}^t\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}\}_{t\leq T}$ is a \emph{game-theoretic supermartingale} if for all $t< T$ and situations $s\in\mathcal{Y}^t$, we have 
  \begin{align}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] \leq X_t(s)~,
  \end{align}
  and a \emph{game-theoretic martingale} if $\textsf{\textbf{E}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] = X_t(s)$.

