[Proposition prop:lbm-response-realization of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm LBM}$ and every $u,v$ in a common
positive eigenspace of $A_\mu$,
\begin{equation}
 \Theta_\mu(u,v)=uv\,\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D).

\end{equation}
The map $U_\mu=U_D$ in (equation eq:lbm-response-space of the paper) is linear and
injective, and
\begin{equation}
 \inner{U_\mu\sigma}{f}_{H}
 =\int_Df\,d\sigma,
 \qquad
 \sigma\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D),\quad f\in C_c^\infty(D).

\end{equation}
Thus the LBM response is faithfully potential-realizable in the sense of
Definition~(def:response-realization of the paper).

[Theorem 106 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] \cite[Thm. 2.5]{Tappe}
Let $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times W,D(A))$ and $$f \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times H, L(U,D(A^2)))$$ be mappings such that
\begin{align*}
&f_0|_{[0,T] \times D(A)} \in \Lip([0,T] \times D(A),D(A^2)),
\\ &f|_{[0,T] \times D(A)} \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times D(A), L(U,D(A^3))).
\end{align*}
Then for every $\xi \in D(A^2)$ there exists a unique mild solution $$(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \beta}([0,T],W)$$ to the random RPDE \eqref{RPDE-fractional} with $Y_0 = \xi$ on $N^c$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem macro-bridge-gen-conc of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Fix $\varepsilon\in(0,1/2)$ and $y\in\mathds{R}$. Recall the definition of $\mathfrak{s}_0, \mathfrak{s}_1$ in~(equation eq:s0-s1-def of the paper). For $\gd\in(0,1/\theta)$ and $i\in\{1,2\}$, define
\begin{align*}
 \mathrm{Bad}_{i,n}(s;\gd)
 :=
 \left\{
 v\in\mathcal{C}_i(s):
 \left|\Gen_i(v)-\frac{s}{\theta}\right|>\gd s
 \right\}.
\end{align*}
Then
\begin{align}
\int_{\mathfrak{s}_0}^{\mathfrak{s}_1}\frac1n
\sum_{\substack{e=\{u,v\}\in\mathcal{B}_s\\
 u\in\mathcal{C}_1(s),\ v\in\mathcal{C}_2(s)}}
A_e(s)^{\theta-1}
\mathds{1}\big\{
 u\in\mathrm{Bad}_{1,n}(s;\gd)
\text{ or }
 v\in\mathrm{Bad}_{2,n}(s;\gd)
\big\}
\,\mathrm d s
\stackrel{\pr}{\to}0.
\end{align}

