[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] For any $N \in \bN$,
\begin{align*}
\sup_{\mu\in \eP(T)} \eF_\beta(X ; \mu)
= \frac{1}{N} \sup_{\bm{\mu}\in \eP(T^N)} \eF_\beta(\bm{X}^N ;  \bm{\mu}).
\end{align*}

