[Lemma l:local_smoothing_homogenized of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:forcing_regularity_iteration of the paper) holds. Fix $\mu>0$, $r\in (1,\infty)$ and $p_0\in (2,p)$. Let $(v^{N,\delta},\pi^{N,\delta},(\widetilde{\pi}^{N,\delta}_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ be a local solution to the stochastic Stokes system (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_quantitative_iteration of the paper) on $Q$ for some $N\geq 1$ and $\delta\in (0,1]$. Let  $(\overline{v}^{N,\delta},\overline{\pi}^{N,\delta})$ be the solution to the homogenized Stokes system (equation eq:homogenized_PDE_linear of the paper) on $(1/2)Q$ provided by Proposition (prop:local_well_posedness_homogenized_SPDE of the paper).
Then there exists a constant $C_0>0$ depending only on $\mu,\varrho,p,q,r,p_0$ and $d$ such that
\begin{equation}

\big(
{\mathbf E}\|\overline{v}^{N,\delta}\|^r_{L^p((1/4)I;W^{1,q}((1/4)B))}\big)^{1/r}
\leq C_0 \mathcal{L}_Q^{\#},
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{L}_Q^{\#}$ is as in (equation eq:def_En_Q of the paper) and $Q=I\times B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

