body:
[Corollary cor:eventwise-hardy of arXiv:2606.25976, 'Gaussian rigidity for infinite exchangeable sequences'] Let $a>0$, let $\gamma_a$ denote the centered Gaussian law $\mathcal{N}(0,a)$ on $\mathbb{R}$, and let $\nu$ be a finite positive Borel measure on $\mathbb{R}$.  Assume that
\begin{equation}
        0\le \nu\le \gamma_a
\end{equation}
as measures, and that
\begin{equation}
        0\le \widehat\nu(t)\le e^{-a t^2/2}
        \qquad\text{for every }t\in\mathbb{R}.
\end{equation}
Then
\[
        \nu=\nu(\mathbb{R})\,\gamma_a.
\]

