[Proposition replace-M-by-explicit-expression-in-tightness-for-critical of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $\Pi$ be a fixed point of BBM with drift $\lambda =\sqrt{2}$ and $\theta \in Dom_{\lambda}(\Pi)$. Then, the random variables $\{\widetilde{Y}_t^b\}_{t\ge 1}$ given by 

\begin{equation}
\widetilde{Y}_t^b := \int_{-\infty}^{\frac{1}{4} \log t }\frac{1}{t^{3/2}}(-x + \log t)e^{\sqrt{2}x} e^{-\frac{x^2}{2t}} \theta(dx)     
\end{equation}
is tight.

