[Lemm l:crossterms of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Fix a Borel set $B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^2)$ and $n\in{\mathbb{Z}_{\geqslant0}}$.
    For all $f,g\in L^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{2n})$ with $f,g\geqslant 0$ almost everywhere,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{E}\left[I_{n}(f\1_{B}^{\otimes n})I_{n}(g\1_{B}^{\otimes n})\right] 
        &\leqslant \mathbb{E}\left[I_{n}(f)I_{n}(g)\right].
    \end{align*}

