[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\psi \in \mathbf{\Psi}$ be a non-strict generator, $A \in \mathcal{A}$, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$, $\fg^0$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_g_t}, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R} and $g^R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_f}. Then the following assertions hold:
\begin{itemize}
        \item[$(i)$] $L_{\psi,A}^0 = \{(x,y) \in \mathbb{I}^2 \colon y \leq \fg^{0}(x)\} \cup (\{0\} \times [\ff^R(0),1])$;
