body:
[Lemma lem:finite-part-remainder-trace of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Fix $V_m$ and the atlas radius $\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}$, so $\partial\Omega\cap B_{\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}(V_m)$ consists only of the two incident ray segments $x=V_m+\sidedistat{m}{i}\tphys{m}{i}$, $\sidedistat{m}{i}=\abs{x-V_m}\in(0,\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}})$, $i=1,2$. Let $\mathcal R_{m,i}\in C^1((0,\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}])$ be the restriction of a residual boundary trace to ray $i$, and suppose for some $\sigma>0$, $B\in\mathbb N_0$,
\begin{align}
 M_{\rm tr}
 &:=
 \max_{i=1,2}\sup_{0<\sidedistat{m}{i}<\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}
 \Big(
 \abs{\mathcal R_{m,i}(\sidedistat{m}{i})}
 +\sidedistat{m}{i}
  \babs{\partial_{\sidedistat{m}{i}}
       \mathcal R_{m,i}(\sidedistat{m}{i})}
 \Big)
 \sidedistat{m}{i}^{-\sigma}
 (1+\abs{\ln \sidedistat{m}{i}})^{-B}
 <\infty.

\end{align}
Then $\mathcal R_{m,i}(\sidedistat{m}{i})\to0$ as $\sidedistat{m}{i}\to0$, $i=1,2$, so the piecewise trace $\mathcal R(V_m+\sidedistat{m}{i}\tphys{m}{i}):=\mathcal R_{m,i}(\sidedistat{m}{i})$, $\mathcal R(V_m):=0$, belongs locally to $H^{\frac{1}{2}}$ across the vertex, with $\nm{\mathcal R}_{H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\partial\Omega\cap B_{\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}(V_m))}\le C_{\sigma,B,\omega_m,\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}M_{\rm tr}$. If this holds at every vertex and the residual trace is $H^1$ on the parts of the open sides away from the vertices, then $\mathcal R\in H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\partial\Omega)$.

