[Corollary 26 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Control on Marginal Edge Probabilities}

    For $\mu^p := \Phi\inv(p) \cdot \diagonal{\Sigma}^{1/2}$ where $p \in (0,1)$ and $\Phi : \R \to [0,1]$ is the standard Gaussian CDF,
    \begin{align*}
        \P((i,j) \in E(X)) = p
        \quad \text{for all $(i,j) \in [n]^2$ where $i<j$}. 
    \end{align*}

