body:
[Proposition 6 (Exact ordered tuple formula) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] If \(K\le n\) and
\(k_i+r_i-1\le\binom{k_i}{2}\) for every \(i\), then
\begin{equation}
  L_n(\mathbf k,\mathbf r)=\frac{(n)_K}{\prod_{i=1}^q k_i!}\prod_{i=1}^q c(k_i,k_i+r_i-1)\,p_n^{K+R-q}(1-p_n)^{A},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  A
  &=K(n-K)
    +\sum_{1\le i<j\le q}k_ik_j
    +\sum_{i=1}^q
      \left\{\binom{k_i}{2}-(k_i+r_i-1)\right\}
  \\
  &=Kn-\frac{K^2}{2}-\frac{3K}{2}-R+q.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
If the feasibility conditions fail, then \(L_n(\mathbf k,\mathbf r)=0\).

[Lem eq:conf_theta_2 of arXiv:2609.01458, 'Confluence relations for $q$-analogues of multiple zeta values'] We have
\begin{equation}
\pi(\left.\Theta(\boldsymbol{k})\right|_{z=1})=0\qquad(\boldsymbol{k}\in\operatorname{Ind}_{\mathrm{BZ}}\setminus\{\emptyset\})
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\pi(\left.T(\Theta(\boldsymbol{k}))\right|_{z=1})=b_{\rho(\boldsymbol{k})}\qquad(\boldsymbol{k}\in\operatorname{Ind}_{\mathrm{BZ}}),
\end{equation}
where $\rho\colon\operatorname{Ind}_{\mathrm{BZ}}\to\operatorname{Ind}_{\mathrm{SZ}}$
is the map defined by 
\[
\rho((k_{1},\dots,k_{d}))=(k_{1}-1,\dots,k_{d}-1).
\]

