[Definition smoothing-est of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] A smoothing on a scale of Banach spaces $(H^{m},\left\| \cdot \right\|_{m})_{m\in \mathbb{R}_{+}}$ is a family of operators
    $(J^{\eta})_{\eta \in (0,1]}$, approximating the identity such that for all $\eta \in (0,1]$:
    \begin{equ}
        \left\| J^\eta-I \right\|_{\mathcal{L}(H^l;H^j)}\leq C\eta^{l-j}  \hbox{ for }  l>j, \qquad 
        \left\| J^\eta \right\|_{\mathcal{L}(H^j;H^l)}\leq C\eta^{-(l-j)} \hbox{ for }  l \geq j.
    \end{equ}

[Theorem theor_pot_wiener of arXiv:2606.27549, 'On Analytically Tractable Multidimensional Diffusions via Doob $h$-Transforms, with Resett'] The diffusion process having infinitesimal moments ((mom_infinitesimali_fx of the paper)) satisfies the SDE ((NEWsde_x_trasf of the paper)) with potential 

   \begin{equation}
   U({\bf x})=-{\bf m}\cdot {\bf x}^\top-\frac{\log(h_c({\bf x}))}{r_1}\ {\bf r}\cdot  a_{*,1} +k, 
   \qquad {\bf x} \in \mathbb{R}^n,\;\; k \in \mathbb{R},

   \end{equation}

with $h_c({\bf x})$ given in ((3.3generica of the paper)), provided that ${\bf r}$
satisfies  condition ((3.4generica of the paper)), such that 
${\bf r}\neq {\bf 0}$ and 

   \begin{equation}
       r_1\ {\bf r}\cdot A-\left({\bf r}\cdot  {a}_{*,1}\right) \  {\bf r}={\bf 0}.

   \end{equation}

