[Theorem T.R1 of arXiv:2509.20657, 'Scaling limit for Brownian motions \\ on the $l$-level Sierpinski gaskets: \\ The fractal '] There exist constants $c_1$ and $\gamma'>0$, independent of $l$, such that if $h_l$ is bounded and harmonic for $({\cal E}_{l}, {\cal F}_{l})$ in a ball $B(x_0,2r)$ for some $x_0\in \mathrm{SG}(l)$ and $r\in (8l^{-1},\tfrac14)$, then
\begin{equation}
\left|h_l(x)-h_l(y)\right|\leq c_1\left(\frac{|x-y|\vee l^{-1}}{r}\right)^{\gamma'}\|h_l\|_\infty, \qquad \forall x,y\in B(x_0,r)\cap \mathrm{SG}(l).
\end{equation}

