body:
[Proposition 12 (Lemma 8.6 of \cite{Gubinelli:06}) of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] For any \(\phi \in C^{N}\), defining \(\phi(\mathbf{Y})\) by
  \[\phi(\mathbf{Y}) = \sum_{f \in \CF_{N - 1}} \partial^f_X \phi(\mathbf{Y}) f\]
  where
  \begin{equation}
    \partial^f_X \phi(\mathbf{Y}) = \sum_{\tau_1 \cdots \tau_{\# f} = f} \frac{1}{(\# f)!}D^{\# f}
    \phi(Y)[(\partial^{\tau_i}_X Y)_{i = 1}^{\# f}]
  \end{equation}
  for any \(f \in \CF_{N - 1}\), we have that \(\phi(\mathbf{Y})\) is
  also a controlled rough path against \(\mathbf{X}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

