body:
[Lemma lem:morlift of arXiv:2609.00978, 'Towards Categorical K\"ahler Geometry'] Let $X\in\cD$, $\overline{Y}\in\cC$, and $\bar{f}\colon GX\to \overline{Y}$ be a morphism.
Suppose that there are:
\begin{enumerate}[(1)]
    \item objects $Y_n\in\cD$ and morphisms $f_n\colon GY_n\to\overline{Y}$, $n\geq 0$,
    \item bicartesian squares
        \[
        \begin{tikzcd}
            FGY_n\arrow[r,"F(f_n)"]\arrow[d,swap,"\varepsilon_{Y_n}"] & F\overline{Y} \arrow[d] \\
            Y_n\arrow[r] & Y_{n+1}
        \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        for $n\geq -1$ (set $Y_{-1}\coloneqq X$, $f_{-1}\coloneqq \bar{f}$),
\end{enumerate}
such that, for $n\geq 0$, $f_n$ is a left homotopy inverse to the morphism $\overline{Y}\xrightarrow{\eta_{\overline{Y}}}GF\overline Y\to GY_n$.
Then $\bar{f}$ lifts along $G$ in the sense that there is a $Y\in \cD$, $f\colon X\to Y$, and an isomorphism $GY\simeq \overline{Y}$ under which $G(f)$ corresponds to a morphism homotopic to $\bar{f}$.

