and in particular almost surely there exists an $n_0(T,k)$ such that $\sup_{t \in [0,T]} |a_j^{(n)}(t)-\tilde{a}_j^{(n)}(t)|\leq C(T,k)\frac{\log(n)^j}{\sqrt{n}}$ for all $n \geq n_0(T,k)$. An ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:6537a791d5448569ea39becef16367d6cc1af674ea6b2ddf93719fb0f3ae02a5","revision_digest":"sha256:800cec4b6578f02a361e3cbcf9484768f5f98ffe4fe0903a066bde630a11c6fa","source_id":"arxiv:2411.01633","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

