[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let a centered stationary Gaussian process $(X_t)_{t\in T}$ be given. Then, for any $\mu \in \eP(T)$,
  \begin{align*}
\eF_\beta(P_X;\mu) \le \eF_\beta(P_X; \su_T),
  \end{align*}
  where $\su_T$ is the uniform probability measure on $T$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def_wtM of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Define the spectral domain $\mathbf D(\tau):=\{z=E+\mathrm{i} \eta\in \mathbb{C} :|z|\le \tau^{-1}, |\eta| \ge N^{-1+\tau}\}$ for an arbitrarily small constant $\tau>0$.
For $z_1,z_2\in \mathbf D(\tau)$, we define the $D\times D$ matrices $\widehat M$ and $L$ as
\begin{align}
    \widehat M_{ab}(z_1,z_2,\Lambda):=D\langle M(z_1) E_{a} M(z_2) E_{b}\rangle ,\quad L_{ab}(z_1,z_2, H, \Lambda):= D\langle G(z_1)E_{a}G(z_2)E_{b}\rangle , 
\end{align}
for  $a,b\in \llbracket D\rrbracket$, and define the $D\times D$ matrix $K$ as

\begin{align}   K(z_1,z_2, \Lambda ):= \left[1-\widehat M(z_1,z_2,\Lambda)\right]^{-1} \widehat M(z_1,z_2,\Lambda).
\end{align}

