[Lemma mainlemma3 of arXiv:2605.28204, 'Estimates of $mm$-entropy of a stable L\'evy process\footnote{Work supported by grant no. '] For all $B>2\alpha$ and $\de > 0$ there exists a constant $K_2 >0$ such that for all small $\ep$ 
    one can find a finite net $\mathcal Y_\ep$ of size not exceeding $\exp(K_2\ep^{-\alpha}|\ln \ep|)$ and satisfying
\begin{equation}   
       \max_{y \in \mathcal Y_\ep } \   \omega(y,2\ep^{B}) \le   2\ep
\end{equation}
and    
\begin{equation*}
            \mathbb{P}\big( \min_{y\in \mathcal Y_\ep} ||X_\ep - y||_\infty > 3 \ep\big) \le \de.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Pro Prop_diff_strongly_convex of arXiv:2606.22183, 'Expected loss of quasi-arithmetic means of exchangeable random variables'] Let $I\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ be a nonempty open interval, $\alpha:(I-I)\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be an even function, and $L:I\to \mathbb{R}$ be a differentiable function.
Then $L$ is strongly $\alpha$-convex if and only if 
 \begin{align}
  L(x)\geqslant L(y) + L'(y)(x-y) + \alpha(x-y),\qquad x,y\in I.
 \end{align}

[Lemma lem:G5b of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] There exists $C_H<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}

  M_2
  =\frac{\sigma^2}{2a}\frac{\gamma}{N}
  +O_H\left(\frac{\gamma^2}{N}+\gamma^3\right).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, the nonlinear correction to the stationary second moment has no unresolved $N^0\gamma^2$ term.

