{"artifact_digest":"sha256:9ad97f77d5b72dd854893656004a5a61b49fa85c04bb0286e08fbd3d68e10ffd","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/9a/9ad97f77d5b72dd854893656004a5a61b49fa85c04bb0286e08fbd3d68e10ffd.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:a4feeb3b54302da7b57b3536df37d5bcdb52eb38412d276dafdd7835967992a5","bundle_entry_key":"2512-06640-lemma-30-non-amenable-number-of-points","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_022","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_022.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2512-06640-lemma-30-non-amenable-number-of-points","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Our strategy is to compare $\{Y(s)\}_{s\geq0}$ to its discretized version, which we are able to apply Lemma (lemma: spectral_lower_bound_of_escape_probability of the paper) to. We now describe this discretization. 

    Given a positive real number $z$, we define the \textit{$z$-walk} as the discrete-time random walk $\{ X^{(z)}(n) \}_{n \geq 0}$ with $X^{(z)}(n) := Y(nz)$. Observe that the transition matrix of the $z$-walk is given by $\mathrm{Q}^{(z)} := e^{z(\mathrm{P}-I)}$. 
    In particular, when $z=1$ we have that 
    \begin{equation}
