[Definition def:ap1:wp of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] A family of measures $\{\mu_t\}_{t \in [0, T]}$ is a weak solution to (equation eq:ap1:formalPDE of the paper) with drift $f$ and initial condition $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ if for all $\phi \in C^{2, 1}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m_T) \cap C(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \times [0, T))$ such that there exists $R \in (0, \infty)$ such that for all $t \in [0, T]$ and $x \not \in B_R$, we have $\phi_t(x) = 0$,  we have
\begin{equation*}
    \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \phi_t(x) \mu_t(dx) = \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \phi_0(x) \mu_0(dx) + \int_0^t \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d} (\partial_s \phi_s(x) + \Delta _s\phi(x) - f_s(x) \cdot \nabla \phi_s(x) )\mu_s(dx) ds
\end{equation*}
for almost every $t \in [0, T]$. We let $\mu(dt, dx) := \mu_t(dx) dt$ denote such a weak solution.

