		\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n |\dot{A}_i^n(t)|^2 = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n |n b_i^n(\floor{nt})|^2 = n |\bm{b}^n(\floor{nt})|_2^2.
	\end{equation*}
	By Lemma~(lemma:drift-vector:a-priori-bound of the paper), the right-hand side is bounded by 1, and it follows that ${\mathbb P}$-almost surely, the empirical measure $\hat{\mu}_n^A$ is contained in $\mathcal{K}_1$. That $\mathcal{K}_1$ is compact is essentially a consequence of the Arzel\`a--Ascoli theorem; see Lemma~(lemma:compactness-K of the ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:0a05808db492e65240ddac34b9d2e335660fb90544861d4387ee54152f1d37e1","revision_digest":"sha256:848e4f321b6d716e419668445a6546874ef21864ed3419a798c00e4afbd97be8","source_id":"arxiv:2605.14149","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

body:
[Proposition prop:reductiontohzero of arXiv:2609.03980, 'Decay Rates and Domain Dependence of a Coupled Wave-Heat System with Spatially Dependant H'] Let $(\Omega,\Omega_w,\Omega_h)$ be a Lipschitz interface triple and let $p:\mathbb{R} \to [0,\infty)$ be a weight function satisfying $p(\lambda)\lesssim |\lambda|$ for all $|\lambda|\gg 1.$ 
    If the generator $A_S^\perp$ of the coupled wave-heat system~(equation eq:1 of the paper) satisfies the residual estimate
    \begin{align*}
        \|(\lambda i +A_S^\perp  )f\|_{\mathbb{H}_1} \gtrsim p(\lambda) \|f\|_{\mathbb{H}_1}, ~~ |\lambda|\gg1,\lambda\in \mathbb{R}
    \end{align*}
    for every $f = (w_1,w_2,h_1)  \in \operatorname{dom}\left(A_S^\perp\right)$ with $h_1=0$, then $A_S^\perp$ even satisfies the estimate
    \begin{align*}
        \|(\lambda i +A_S^\perp  )f\|_{\mathbb{H}_1} \gtrsim \left(\frac{p(\lambda)}{|\lambda|}\right)^2 \|f\|_{\mathbb{H}_1},~~ |\lambda|\gg1,\lambda\in \mathbb{R}
    \end{align*}
    for all $f \in \operatorname{dom}\left(A_S^\perp\right)$.

