{"artifact_digest":"sha256:eec91aa18c3b562a6d6407d5efc8f280ca8086e686241df41c6bd5dbc10632c1","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/ee/eec91aa18c3b562a6d6407d5efc8f280ca8086e686241df41c6bd5dbc10632c1.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:927afb676ae68f04ff269bf2890ea471aa6c7d98f43063cd34f03e1dbddf9ae5","bundle_entry_key":"pairs","bundle_id":"population.probability-variance-joint-laws-and-voronoi-partials-007","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"codex-probability-01a07a40/bundle_007.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.measure:stationary-even-parity-triples-pairwise-not-joint-independence","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Even agreement of every one- and two-site marginal need not identify a measure. On Z, partition into triples with a uniformly random phase and use iid uniform even-parity bit triples (000,011,101,110). Every pair of distinct bits is independent Bernoulli(1/2), including pairs across triples. The measure is translation invariant. For three consecutive sites, however, the all-ones probability is (1/3)*0+(2/3)*(1/8)=1/12, whereas iid Bernoulli(1/2) gives 1/8. Thus the pair-correlation experiments cannot distinguish all possible candidate laws.

Second check: For an aligned triple, 111 is forbidden. In each nonaligned phase the triple crosses a block boundary; two bits from one block are independent and the third is independent of them, giving 1/8. Averaging the three phases gives 1/12.

Limit: Need a coupling or a characterization using all cylinder events. This auxiliary counterexample refutes only the proposed inference from pair data, not equality of the actual ARW limits.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:fe56473d9868d2782c2a89777340b484cd00d87a0d02c3b14bb0ec55ac348696","revision_digest":"sha256:84e03ae90d65099dadd671e5c38ee2055efa728519f0a5dfa600780f69ede998","source_id":"owner-probability-exposition-20260907:pairs","source_revision":"author-checked-private-20260907-v1","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

