[Lemma lem:euclidWeyl of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $\alpha\in [0,1]$ and $\beta_\ell=o(\alpha \ell)$ as above. 
If $M=\mathbb{R}^n$, for any $k\in \mathbb{N}$, the error $\delta^{\mathbb{R}^n}_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}=\delta^{\mathbb{R}^n}_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}(\alpha,\mathcal{C}^k,[0,\rho_\ell])$ in the scaling bound (equation eq:scalimRW of the paper) satisfies
\begin{gather}
\delta_{[\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}

={\mathrm{O}(1)\begin{cases}
    \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell} & n\ge 3

    \\



    m_\ell \sqrt{\frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}} 
    & n =2 
    \\

    m_\ell^2& n =1
\end{cases}
}
\\
\delta_{ [\alpha\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}=O\left( \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}
\right),\  \text{if $\alpha\in [0,1)$}.
\end{gather}
in bounded range $0\le \rho_\ell \le \mathrm{diam}(M)$, as $\ell\to+\infty$. In particular, if $n\ge 2$, then $\delta_{[\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}=\mathrm{o}(1)$.

