{"artifact_digest":"sha256:39e7a450ec1c73730d64eecf33ad54ab03b94966ac736af50e5a2d1793f71682","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/39/39e7a450ec1c73730d64eecf33ad54ab03b94966ac736af50e5a2d1793f71682.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:eee30f1f64a211b5ee2c369ce58e96f2aee6994a5a9c9030d8ee88272b012b0e","bundle_entry_key":"no-local","bundle_id":"population.harvest-strictness-corrections-20260909","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"codex-overnight-corrections-20260908/bundle_005.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.epidemics:no-local-contacts-defeat-strict-household-monotonicity","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Consider the contact model with X_L=0 almost surely and X_G Poisson with mean 2. There are no local contacts to replace. For any fixed finite population, couple all choices of household partition and replacement probability using exactly the same global contact graph and initial infectives. The infection process is then identical path by path. Household size and replacement probability do not enter any transition.

Consequently the limiting major-outbreak probability and limiting final fraction, whenever defined, are constant in those two parameters. The local pgf is identically 1 and its logarithm is convex. The example is not merely a zero-epidemic edge case: the global offspring mean is 2, and its extinction fixed-point equation q=exp(2(q-1)) has a solution below 1. Indeed the right side minus q is positive at 0 and negative at 1/2, since e^-1<1/2. The usual positive final-size solution obeys z=1-exp(-2z). Neither equation contains household size or replacement probability.

This disproves the universal strictness asserted in both harvested epidemic notes. It does not disprove their weak monotonicity statements. A second exact control is p=1: all contacts are global, so the model again has no dependence on household partition. Additionally, household size is integer valued; the harvested final-size proof's expression dz/dh is not a defined derivative for the given model without a separately justified interpolation.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:af81c19ea347d782a053d7203ce8be50dd2350dde22896e3b9926f5b5b933956","revision_digest":"sha256:87d29cf31702c679b42c5fd3275ddae7f13c8c0584edca1e96782d585e2714cb","source_id":"owner-original:harvest-strictness-no-local-20260909","source_revision":"7f01ee78661c5b707977d81b0ddd4bc314377321fa66008c99fed0ef25f76ad1","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

