[Theorem thm:binary-characterization of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] Let $L$ be as in Lemma~(lem:cm-kernel of the paper), and let $\psi\in\cC$ be indecomposable in the sense of Definition~(definition:indecomposable of the paper). Suppose that $\eta_1,\eta_2\in\cC$, and set $f_j(\xi)\coloneqq L(\eta_j(\xi)),$ $j=1,2.$
    If
    \begin{align}
        \Phi_L\bigl(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi)\bigr)=L(\psi(\xi))
        \qquad\text{for all }\xi\in\R,
    \end{align}
    then there exist $a_1,a_2\ge 0$ with $a_1+a_2=1$ such that
    \begin{align}
        f_j(\xi)=L(a_j\psi(\xi)),
        \qquad j=1,2.
    \end{align}

