[Definition Well-behaved Backtracking Intersections for SC Polynomials of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given $\tau \in \mathcal{B}(K)$ that are backbone-dangling shapes, we say the composition $\tau\cdot \tau'$ forms a backtracking intersection if \begin{enumerate}
		\item $U_{\tau} \equiv V_{\tau'} $: the left-boundary vertex of $U_\tau$ matches with the right-boundary vertex of $V_{\tau'}$ ;
		\item $E(\tau) \equiv E(\tau')$: the underlying edge-set of the two sets receive the same labels.  
	\end{enumerate}
	We denote the corresponding backtracking intersection pattern as $\mathsf{BacktrackingInt}(\tau)$.

