[Lemma lem:Bakry-Emery of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] For $H(x)=\frac12 \sum_{i=1}^N\lambda_i x_i^2$,
    \begin{align*}
        -\nabla_{\mathsf{Sp}}^2 H\succeq ((2\lambda_1-\lambda_2-\lambda_N)m^2-(\lambda_1-\lambda_N)) I\,.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, if $\mathsf{m}_{\textsc{e}}>\mathsf{m}_{\textsc{be}}$, then there exists $\kappa_{\textsc{be}}>0$ such that 
    \begin{align*}
        -\nabla_{\mathsf{Sp}}^2 H+\frac1\beta \mathrm{Ric}_{\mathsf{Sp}}\succeq\kappa_{\textsc{be}} I\,.
    \end{align*}
    in the region $\mathcal D=\mathbf{S}_N\cap \{|m(x)|>\mathsf{m}_{1}\}$.

