[Theorem thm:infvol2pt of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $d \ge 4$,  $\eta \in [0,1/2)$,  $L$ be sufficiently large and $g>0$ be sufficiently small.
Then there exists $\nu_c  \equiv \nu_c (g) = O(g)$ such that
\begin{align}
	\lim_{N\rightarrow \infty} \langle \varphi_{\sf o}^{(1)} \varphi_{\sf x}^{(1)} \rangle_{g,\nu_c,  N} =: \langle \varphi_{\sf o}^{(1)} \varphi_{\sf x}^{(1)} \rangle_{g,\nu_c,  \Z^d} =: \C_{\sf x}
\end{align}
exists and satisfies 
\begin{align}
	\C_{\sf x} \sim c_1 |{\sf x}|^{-(d-2+\eta)} \quad \text{as} \quad |{\sf x}| \rightarrow \infty 
\end{align}
for some constant $c_1$ such that $c_1 = \gamma(d,\eta) + O(g)$ when $\eta = 0$ and $c_1 = \gamma(d,\eta)$ when $\eta \neq 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

