[Theo 8 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M, J, \omega)$ be an lck manifold and assume $\omega$ is Gauduchon satisfying the second Bismut--Einstein equation
    \begin{equation*}
        \Ric^{B, 2}=f \omega, \qquad \text{for some}\, f \in \mathcal{C}^{\infty}(M).
    \end{equation*}
    If $\mathrm{dim}_{\mathbb{C}}M\geq 4$, then $\omega$ is Vaisman and $f \equiv 0$.   If $\mathrm{dim}_{\mathbb{C}}M \in \{2, 3\}$ and $f \geq 0$, then $\omega$ is Vaisman and $f\equiv 0$.

